    "https://www.uvmjobs.com/postings/88644": {
      "title": "Post-Award Research Administration Partner",
      "description": "University of Vermont Employment Opportunities | Post-Award Research Administration Partner Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UVM Employee Wellness Human Resources UVM Cultural Resource Guide FAQ Clery Act Reports Post-Award Research Administration Partner Please carefully review the details of this position below. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job button (or see the Special Instructions below if no button appears). If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark button. The University of Vermont is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, or any other category legally protected by federal or state law. For information on safety and security at the University of Vermont, see the annual security report by clicking on the Clery Act button in the sidebar menu. Finalists for positions at UVM may be subject to a criminal background check. For classified staff positions, actual hiring pay dependent on current competitor market conditions, comparable campus peer(s) at time of hire, and candidate’s experience level and length. Be sure to carefully review and update your application information before submitting an application! Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Details Advertising/Posting Title Post-Award Research Administration Partner Posting Summary This position is eligible for 100% remote work. Post-Award Research Administration Partner – Position Summary This position provides comprehensive post-award financial administration and compliance oversight for sponsored projects from setup through closeout. The role ensures accurate budget management, monitoring of expenditures, financial forecasting, effort allocation, and adherence to sponsor and university requirements. The Post-Award Analyst serves as a primary resource for Principal Investigators and departments, partners closely with SPA Financial Analysts, and contributes to PI onboarding and training initiatives. This position is eligible for 100% remote work. Budget Analysis & Compliance Interpret sponsor regulations and coordinate with PIs to ensure compliance with award terms and conditions. Facilitate regular budget meetings with PIs and research staff to support compliant project management. Monitor award budgets, track unobligated balances, and prepare expenditure projections. Review project expenditures to ensure costs are allowable, reasonable, allocable, and consistent. Monitor and verify cost share commitments in alignment with sponsor and university guidelines. Ensure deliverables and required reports are completed and submitted in accordance with sponsor requirements. Effort Management Oversee effort reporting and related compliance to meet federal and university standards. Prepare and process salary distributions based on PI requests and effort review outcomes. Provide guidance and training to PIs on effort regulations, requirements, and best practices. Advise department leadership on PI funding status, anticipated support concerns, and potential conflicts of commitment. Financial Management Serve as a primary point of contact for PIs needing financial and administrative support during the post-award period. Coordinate with SPA Award Acceptance to establish internal projects and subawards at the time of award. Ensure project setup, including cost share, is completed accurately. Review suspense accounts and initiate timely cost transfers. Prepare and submit cost transfers in accordance with policy and sponsor requirements. Work with departments to resolve budget errors and request rebudget actions within sponsor authority. Support audit activities and site visits, collaborating with PIs and SPA compliance staff as needed. Minimum Qualifications (or equivalent combination of education and experience) Education and work experience: Bachelor’s Degree Finance, Business Administration or Accounting Relevant Work Experience 2-4 years Competencies: Accounting and budgeting skills in managing complex financial accounts and funds, as well as knowledge of generally accepted accounting, fiscal, and reporting principles. Working knowledge of contracts and grants transactions and applicable financial systems, as well as related policy requirements. Demonstrated working knowledge of applicable federal, state, local, sponsor, and institutional regulations, policies, and guidelines. Ability to work independently and as a team member, research and resolve problems, meet deadlines, and follow through on assignments with minimal direction. Independent judgment and strong organization and communication skills and customer service focus across broad and diverse subject areas. Desirable Qualifications 3-5 years demonstrated experience in research contract and grant management. Certified Research Administration ( CRA ) or Certified Financial Research Administration ( CFRA ) designation. Anticipated Pay Range $69,000 - $78,000 Other Information Special Conditions A probationary period may be required, This position is eligible for a hybrid schedule with an option to split time between campus and elsewhere, in accordance with the university telecommuting policy, This position is eligible for full-time telework in accordance with the university telecommuting policy, Background Check required for this position FLSA Exempt Union Position Yes, UVMSU Posting Details Position will be posted for a minimum of one week, after which it is subject to removal without notice. Job Location Burlington, Vermont, United States Job Open Date 10/20/2026 Job Close Date (Jobs close at 11:59 PM EST.) Open Until Filled No Our Common Ground Statement The University of Vermont is a welcoming, educationally purposeful community committed to creating an inclusive environment that embraces intellectual diversity and global perspectives. We seek to prepare students to be accountable leaders who will bring to their work a grasp of complexity, effective problem-solving and communication skills, and an enduring commitment to learning and ethical conduct. Members of the University of Vermont community embrace and advance the values of Our Common Ground: Respect, Integrity, Innovation, Openness, Justice, and Responsibility. Staff play a critical role in this effort and the successful candidate will demonstrate a strong commitment to UVM’s mission and advancing Our Common Ground values through the execution of their job duties. Position Information Position Title Research Administration PC3 X Posting Number S6369PO Department Sponsored Project Admin/30612 Position Number 00025843 Percent of Full-Time 1.0 Standard Hours at 1.0 FTE 37.5 Term (months per year) 12 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Chronicle of Higher Education HigherEdJobs Inside Higher Ed LinkedIn Seven Days UVM Employee (Please specify below) UVM Employment Web Site Vermont JobLink (Department of Labor) Other (Please specify below) * Please specify here where applicable. Enter \"NA\" if not applicable. (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application Optional Documents ©2019 The University of Vermont – Burlington, VT 05405 – (802) 656-3131 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
