    "https://www.uvmjobs.com/postings/88640": {
      "title": "Agroecology Research Specialist",
      "description": "University of Vermont Employment Opportunities | Agroecology Research Specialist Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UVM Employee Wellness Human Resources UVM Cultural Resource Guide FAQ Clery Act Reports Agroecology Research Specialist Please carefully review the details of this position below. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job button (or see the Special Instructions below if no button appears). If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark button. The University of Vermont is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, or any other category legally protected by federal or state law. For information on safety and security at the University of Vermont, see the annual security report by clicking on the Clery Act button in the sidebar menu. Finalists for positions at UVM may be subject to a criminal background check. For classified staff positions, actual hiring pay dependent on current competitor market conditions, comparable campus peer(s) at time of hire, and candidate’s experience level and length. Be sure to carefully review and update your application information before submitting an application! Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Details Advertising/Posting Title Agroecology Research Specialist Posting Summary This position is responsible for assisting with ecological and livestock related research operations and data collection at the Food Systems Research Institute and the Food Systems Research Station at Nordic Farm and for laboratory analysis and manuscript development on UVM’s campus. This position is located at the co-located University of Vermont ( UVM ) and USDA -Agricultural Research Service ( ARS ) Food Systems Research Institute and Food Systems Research Units, in Burlington, VT with substantial workload at the Food Systems Research Station at Nordic Farm located in Charlotte, VT. The UVM Food Systems Research Institute and the USDA - ARS Food Systems Research Unit are staffed with personnel consisting of research scientists, scientific support staff, student trainees, and administrative support staff. Scientists and research support personnel explore diverse subject matter expertise spanning the food system and farm research projects that include livestock and forage capacity modeling of regional livestock and nutrient flows as well as beef and sheep production, welfare, and behavior research. The collaboration also spans agronomy, food safety, and human dimensions research. The location has multiple work sites located within Chittenden County. The location and its worksites encompass 400 acres of leased land and 900 acres of owned land that include multiple research laboratories, farm and field plots for experimental work on major crops grown within the region, facilities for housing heavy duty machinery and other equipment, and facilities for housing animals involved in livestock research. Farming operations primarily support the production of beef cows, calves, and finish steers; in addition, operations support crops for research on livestock forages and small grains for human consumption. Minimum Qualifications (or equivalent combination of education and experience) This position requires significant teamwork, technical experience, and effective communication with other members of the Forage and Livestock research group. A combination of formal and experiential education is required: Bachelor’s degree in a related field with at least one year of experience working in ecological and food systems research. In field experience should include working as a research technician with experience collecting in-field forage and livestock data. Incumbent should be proficient in GIS systems and will have basic knowledge of spreadsheet management. Valid driver’s license or ability to obtain, and driver’s check required. Skill in working with individuals from diverse cultures or backgrounds sufficient to work with and motivate others and to train student interns who perform farm duties. Skill in communicating both orally and in writing to provide guidance and instruction to employees, to discuss changes for plans and work projects, interface with the public, and to keep UVM / USDA partners informed of critical needs. Must possess strong organizational skills. Demonstrated knowledge of applying a wide range of data management and collection techniques of forage and livestock data, including (a) techniques for safely handling and herding livestock, implementing feedlot data collection strategies, and implementing grazing and rotational grazing forage data collection protocols; (b) keeping detailed herd management, GIS and weather station, and forage records; © methods for recycling and composting of organic end products as related to farm operations; and (d) methods for water and energy conservation as related to farm operations. Mechanical aptitude to operate, maintain, calibrate, and repair field and laboratory research equipment. Working knowledge of rules, regulations, and practical requirements related to livestock management, including workplace safety, and land and water stewardship. Working knowledge of Microsoft Office applications such as Word, Excel, Outlook, and OneDrive. This includes the use of spreadsheets for data management and for some budget and financial management purposes and the documentation of all field operations in a way that is accessible and usable by researchers. Desirable Qualifications Anticipated Pay Range $25.13 - $27.18 Other Information $49,000 – $53,000 Special Conditions Weekend work required, Non-standard work hours required, A probationary period may be required, Contingent on continued funding, Occasional evening and/or weekends required (if non-exempt position, may result in overtime), Travel to and from worksites required, Background Check required for this position FLSA Non-Exempt Union Position Yes, UVMSU Posting Details Position will be posted for a minimum of one week, after which it is subject to removal without notice. Job Location Location listed in Advertising Copy or Other Information Job Open Date 10/20/2026 Job Close Date (Jobs close at 11:59 PM EST.) Open Until Filled No Our Common Ground Statement The University of Vermont is a welcoming, educationally purposeful community committed to creating an inclusive environment that embraces intellectual diversity and global perspectives. We seek to prepare students to be accountable leaders who will bring to their work a grasp of complexity, effective problem-solving and communication skills, and an enduring commitment to learning and ethical conduct. Members of the University of Vermont community embrace and advance the values of Our Common Ground: Respect, Integrity, Innovation, Openness, Justice, and Responsibility. Staff play a critical role in this effort and the successful candidate will demonstrate a strong commitment to UVM’s mission and advancing Our Common Ground values through the execution of their job duties. Position Information Position Title Research Laboratory PC2 N Posting Number S6368PO Department Food Systems Research Institut/30026 Position Number 00028031 Percent of Full-Time 1.0 Standard Hours at 1.0 FTE 37.5 Term (months per year) 12 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application Optional Documents ©2019 The University of Vermont – Burlington, VT 05405 – (802) 656-3131 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.uvmjobs.com/postings/88639": {
      "title": "Special Assistant to the CHRO",
      "description": "University of Vermont Employment Opportunities | Special Assistant to the CHRO Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UVM Employee Wellness Human Resources UVM Cultural Resource Guide FAQ Clery Act Reports Special Assistant to the CHRO Please carefully review the details of this position below. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job button (or see the Special Instructions below if no button appears). If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark button. The University of Vermont is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, or any other category legally protected by federal or state law. For information on safety and security at the University of Vermont, see the annual security report by clicking on the Clery Act button in the sidebar menu. Finalists for positions at UVM may be subject to a criminal background check. For classified staff positions, actual hiring pay dependent on current competitor market conditions, comparable campus peer(s) at time of hire, and candidate’s experience level and length. Be sure to carefully review and update your application information before submitting an application! Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Details Advertising/Posting Title Special Assistant to the CHRO Posting Summary The University of Vermont is seeking a highly organized, adaptable, and trusted professional to serve as Special Assistant to the Chief Human Resources Officer ( CHRO ). In this unique role, you will operate at the center of Human Resources, partnering closely with the CHRO and HR leadership team to advance strategic priorities, support executive decision-making, and ensure the smooth coordination of critical initiatives, communications, and operations. This position combines elements of HR, project management, executive operations, and communications. The Special Assistant serves as a trusted extension of the CHRO , helping manage priorities in a fast-paced environment; preparing presentations, reports, and executive correspondence; coordinating complex schedules and sensitive meetings; and supporting follow-through on key organizational initiatives. The role regularly works with confidential information and requires sound judgment, discretion, and the ability to anticipate needs before they arise. Develop a strong understanding of the CHRO’s communication approach to serve as a trusted extension of the office. Consistently communicate in a manner that fosters trust, preserves relationships, and advances positive working partnerships while effectively conveying decisions, feedback, and sensitive information. The ideal candidate is a relationship builder who thrives in dynamic environments, learns quickly, communicates with polish and professionalism, and enjoys bringing clarity and order to complex challenges. This is an exceptional opportunity for an emerging HR, operations, or administrative professional who is interested in gaining broad exposure to executive leadership, institutional strategy, and the inner workings of a high-performing HR organization. Minimum Qualifications (or equivalent combination of education and experience) Bachelor’s degree and two to five years of progressively responsible experience in human resources, business operations, executive support, project coordination, administration, communications, or a related field; or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Demonstrated experience managing multiple priorities, coordinating complex activities, and meeting deadlines in a fast-paced environment. Strong written communication skills, with experience drafting professional correspondence, reports, presentations, or other business communications. Experience researching, gathering, organizing, and presenting information to support decision-making and problem solving. Demonstrated proficiency with Microsoft Office applications, including Outlook, Word, Excel, and PowerPoint, and the ability to learn new systems and technologies. Experience handling sensitive and confidential information with discretion, sound judgment, and professionalism. Strong organizational, interpersonal, and relationship management skills, with the ability to work effectively with individuals at all levels of an organization. Desirable Qualifications Experience supporting senior leaders, executives, or leadership teams. Experience working in a higher education institution. Experience preparing presentations, briefing materials, dashboards, reports, or executive communications. Knowledge of human resources practices, employment policies, and organizational operations. Experience working with confidential employee relations, labor relations, or personnel matters. Anticipated Pay Range $72,000 to $78,000 Other Information Special Conditions A probationary period may be required, Background Check required for this position FLSA Exempt Union Position No Posting Details Position will be posted for a minimum of one week, after which it is subject to removal without notice. Job Location Burlington, Vermont, United States Job Open Date 10/14/2026 Job Close Date (Jobs close at 11:59 PM EST.) Open Until Filled No Our Common Ground Statement The University of Vermont is a welcoming, educationally purposeful community committed to creating an inclusive environment that embraces intellectual diversity and global perspectives. We seek to prepare students to be accountable leaders who will bring to their work a grasp of complexity, effective problem-solving and communication skills, and an enduring commitment to learning and ethical conduct. Members of the University of Vermont community embrace and advance the values of Our Common Ground: Respect, Integrity, Innovation, Openness, Justice, and Responsibility. Staff play a critical role in this effort and the successful candidate will demonstrate a strong commitment to UVM’s mission and advancing Our Common Ground values through the execution of their job duties. Position Information Position Title Univ Ops Administration PC1 X Posting Number S6360PO Department Human Resources/11305 Position Number 00028029 Percent of Full-Time 1.0 Standard Hours at 1.0 FTE 37.5 Term (months per year) 12 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application Optional Documents ©2019 The University of Vermont – Burlington, VT 05405 – (802) 656-3131 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
