    "https://www.uvmjobs.com/postings/88607": {
      "title": "VCBH Research Lab Assistant",
      "description": "University of Vermont Employment Opportunities | VCBH Research Lab Assistant Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UVM Employee Wellness Human Resources UVM Cultural Resource Guide FAQ Clery Act Reports VCBH Research Lab Assistant Please carefully review the details of this position below. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job button (or see the Special Instructions below if no button appears). If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark button. The University of Vermont is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, or any other category legally protected by federal or state law. For information on safety and security at the University of Vermont, see the annual security report by clicking on the Clery Act button in the sidebar menu. Finalists for positions at UVM may be subject to a criminal background check. For classified staff positions, actual hiring pay dependent on current competitor market conditions, comparable campus peer(s) at time of hire, and candidate’s experience level and length. Be sure to carefully review and update your application information before submitting an application! Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Details Advertising/Posting Title VCBH Research Lab Assistant Posting Summary The Vermont Center on Behavior and Health ( VCBH , https://www.med.uvm.edu/behaviorandhealth/home ) is an interdisciplinary, internationally-recognized research center committed to investigating relationships between personal behavior patterns (i.e., lifestyle) and risk for chronic disease and premature death. VCBH’s work has historically focused on health disparities for the most vulnerable populations, particularly among the socioeconomically disadvantaged, where these risk factors are overrepresented. This position will conduct the day-to-day tasks associated with running research studies testing interventions to reduce substance use and investigating substance use use patterns. Responsibilities include maintaining study databases, participant recruitment, meeting with participants, verifying participant consents, administering questionnaires, conducting interviews, managing study equipment and supplies, and coordinating and conducting remote study procedures. Oversee the distribution of participant compensation and purchase of equipment and supplies. Assist Principal Investigators as needed with research related activities and with IRB -approved protocols and the preparation of progress reports, presentations, and manuscripts. Other duties include maintaining files and records, using discretion regarding sensitive information, and maintaining confidentiality within the framework of the University guidelines. Reports to Principal Investigator and receives functional supervision from other investigators and the project manager. Minimum Qualifications (or equivalent combination of education and experience) Bachelor of Arts or Bachelor of Science degree is required, preferably in a related field such as, psychology, social work, or medical areas and one or more years’ related experience is preferred. Must have experience with the Microsoft Office suite (e.g., Word, Excel, and PowerPoint) and ideally experience or training in data management. Desirable Qualifications Attention to detail and an interest in behavioral health research. Experience in research is desirable and specific experience with study management would be considered a particular strength. Experience working with participants in a research setting is a strength. Anticipated Pay Range $24.00 - $28.00/hour, depending on experience Other Information Special Conditions A probationary period may be required, Contingent on continued funding, Occasional evening and/or weekends required (if non-exempt position, may result in overtime), This position is eligible for a hybrid schedule with an option to split time between campus and elsewhere, in accordance with the university telecommuting policy, Background Check required for this position FLSA Non-Exempt Union Position Yes, UVMSU Posting Details Position will be posted for a minimum of one week, after which it is subject to removal without notice. Job Location Burlington, Vermont, United States Job Open Date 10/15/2026 Job Close Date (Jobs close at 11:59 PM EST.) 10/22/2026 Open Until Filled No Our Common Ground Statement The University of Vermont is a welcoming, educationally purposeful community committed to creating an inclusive environment that embraces intellectual diversity and global perspectives. We seek to prepare students to be accountable leaders who will bring to their work a grasp of complexity, effective problem-solving and communication skills, and an enduring commitment to learning and ethical conduct. Members of the University of Vermont community embrace and advance the values of Our Common Ground: Respect, Integrity, Innovation, Openness, Justice, and Responsibility. Staff play a critical role in this effort and the successful candidate will demonstrate a strong commitment to UVM’s mission and advancing Our Common Ground values through the execution of their job duties. Position Information Position Title Research Laboratory OC2 N Posting Number S6364PO Department Psychiatry/55750 Position Number 00028030 Percent of Full-Time 1.00 Standard Hours at 1.0 FTE 37.5 Term (months per year) 12 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Please specify here where applicable. Enter \"NA\" if not applicable. (Open Ended Question) How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Chronicle of Higher Education HigherEdJobs Inside Higher Ed LinkedIn Seven