    "https://www.uvmjobs.com/postings/88582": {
      "title": "Health Outreach Specialist",
      "description": "University of Vermont Employment Opportunities | Health Outreach Specialist Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UVM Employee Wellness Human Resources UVM Cultural Resource Guide FAQ Clery Act Reports Health Outreach Specialist Please carefully review the details of this position below. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job button (or see the Special Instructions below if no button appears). If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark button. The University of Vermont is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, or any other category legally protected by federal or state law. For information on safety and security at the University of Vermont, see the annual security report by clicking on the Clery Act button in the sidebar menu. Finalists for positions at UVM may be subject to a criminal background check. For classified staff positions, actual hiring pay dependent on current competitor market conditions, comparable campus peer(s) at time of hire, and candidate’s experience level and length. Be sure to carefully review and update your application information before submitting an application! Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Details Advertising/Posting Title Health Outreach Specialist Posting Summary The Health Outreach Specialist will lead implementation of the University of Vermont Cancer Center’s cancer prevention and screening programs across rural Vermont and northern New York, with a primary focus on mobile activities supported through the Rural Health Transformation Fund. Serve as the operational lead for community-based cancer prevention, screening, and outreach initiatives delivered through the UVM Cancer Center’s mobile outreach platform. Working collaboratively with the community outreach and engagement team, clinical staff, community partners, Vermont Free & Referral Clinics, and Cancer Center leadership, develop and implement outreach activities that reduce barriers to cancer prevention and screening, increase access to care, and connect community members with health education, navigation resources, screening services, and follow-up care. Identify outreach opportunities, cultivate community relationships, coordinate community-based screening initiatives, and represent the UVM Cancer Center at events and activities throughout the region. The Outreach Specialist serves as a key member of an interdisciplinary team dedicated to reducing the burden of cancer, especially in rural communities. This position is responsible for planning, implementing, evaluating, and continuously improving clinical outreach activities, ensuring mobile and place-based programs are responsive to community needs and aligned with organizational and grant-funded priorities. Minimum Qualifications (or equivalent combination of education and experience) Minimum Bachelor’s degree plus one to three years of experience in: · Public health · Community health · Human services · Program operations · Event coordination · Healthcare outreach OR equivalent combination of education and experience. Must possess: · Strong organizational skills. · Event coordination experience. · Ability to work independently. · Excellent interpersonal communication skills. · Ability to build productive working relationships with community organizations and stakeholders. · Experience managing multiple priorities in dynamic community-based settings. · Valid driver’s license and acceptable driving record. · Willingness to drive outreach van. · Ability to travel extensively throughout Vermont and northern NY and work occasional evenings and weekends. Desirable Qualifications · Experience with mobile health programs. · Community Health Worker experience or public health training. · Cancer prevention or screening experience. · Experience working with rural populations. · Experience with data collection, program reporting, or public health evaluation activities. · Experience working within healthcare, nonprofit, or community-based organizations. Anticipated Pay Range $62,000 - $67,000 Other Information Special Conditions Non-standard work hours required, A probationary period may be required, Occasional evening and/or weekends required (if non-exempt position, may result in overtime), Travel to and from worksites required, This position is eligible for a hybrid schedule with an option to split time between campus and elsewhere, in accordance with the university telecommuting policy, Background Check required for this position FLSA Exempt Union Position Yes, UVMSU Posting Details Position will be posted for a minimum of one week, after which it is subject to removal without notice. Job Location Burlington, Vermont, United States Job Open Date 10/14/2026 Job Close Date (Jobs close at 11:59 PM EST.) Open Until Filled Yes Our Common Ground Statement The University of Vermont is a welcoming, educationally purposeful community committed to creating an inclusive environment that embraces intellectual diversity and global perspectives. We seek to prepare students to be accountable leaders who will bring to their work a grasp of complexity, effective problem-solving and communication skills, and an enduring commitment to learning and ethical conduct. Members of the University of Vermont community embrace and advance the values of Our Common Ground: Respect, Integrity, Innovation, Openness, Justice, and Responsibility. Staff play a critical role in this effort and the successful candidate will demonstrate a strong commitment to UVM’s mission and advancing Our Common Ground values through the execution of their job duties. Position Information Position Title Community Outreach PC2 X Posting Number S6362PO Department Vermont Cancer Center/55060 Position Number 00028026 Percent of Full-Time 1.0 Standard Hours at 1.0 FTE 37.5 Term (months per year) 12 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application Optional Documents Curriculum Vitae ©2019 The University of Vermont – Burlington, VT 05405 – (802) 656-3131 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
