    "https://www.uvmjobs.com/postings/88567": {
      "title": "Licensing &amp; Communications CSR",
      "description": "University of Vermont Employment Opportunities | Licensing &amp; Communications CSR Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UVM Employee Wellness Human Resources UVM Cultural Resource Guide FAQ Clery Act Reports Licensing & Communications CSR Please carefully review the details of this position below. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job button (or see the Special Instructions below if no button appears). If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark button. The University of Vermont is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, or any other category legally protected by federal or state law. For information on safety and security at the University of Vermont, see the annual security report by clicking on the Clery Act button in the sidebar menu. Finalists for positions at UVM may be subject to a criminal background check. For classified staff positions, actual hiring pay dependent on current competitor market conditions, comparable campus peer(s) at time of hire, and candidate’s experience level and length. Be sure to carefully review and update your application information before submitting an application! Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Details Advertising/Posting Title Licensing & Communications CSR Posting Summary This position serves as Licensing and Communications Coordinator / Customer Service Rep for the Research Center for Children, Youth, and Families ( RCCYF ), publisher of social and behavior assessment tools known as the Achenbach System of Empirically Based Assessment (ASEBA®). Contribute substantively to RCCYF’s nonprofit mission by providing licensing coordination, customer service, and communications development. Prepare and tailor license agreements from standard templates for mental health care providers and researchers licensing the use of ASEBA® products. Communicate with applicants, generate invoices, track status of signatures and customer payments from initial license application through full execution of license agreement. Field questions and requests from customers, licensees, and authorized distributors and provide responsive, thorough, and timely replies by e-mail and phone. Process sales orders through the A/R system and fulfill orders as part of small, cross-functional customer service team. Creatively produce an annual catalog using desktop publishing software. Maintain dynamic websites (including www.aseba.org ) and create enhanced product images for e-commerce site. Edit ASEBA® manuals, guides, and assessment forms for publication, and administratively support the translation review process. Pay bills and deposit customer checks, in a backup capacity. Minimum Qualifications (or equivalent combination of education and experience) Bachelor’s degree in relevant area. One to three years’ customer service experience using Microsoft Word, Microsoft Excel, Adobe InDesign, PhotoShop, and WordPress. Effective verbal and written communication skills, and ability to work independently and collaboratively. Desirable Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in psychology. Experience with QuickBooks and e-commerce. Anticipated Pay Range $24.50 - $27.50/hour Other Information Special Conditions A probationary period may be required, Contingent on continued funding, Occasional evening and/or weekends required (if non-exempt position, may result in overtime), This position is eligible for a hybrid schedule with an option to split time between campus and elsewhere, in accordance with the university telecommuting policy, Background Check required for this position FLSA Non-Exempt Union Position Yes, UVMSU Posting Details Position will be posted for a minimum of one week, after which it is subject to removal without notice. Job Location Burlington, Vermont, United States Job Open Date 10/14/2026 Job Close Date (Jobs close at 11:59 PM EST.) 10/21/2026 Open Until Filled No Our Common Ground Statement The University of Vermont is a welcoming, educationally purposeful community committed to creating an inclusive environment that embraces intellectual diversity and global perspectives. We seek to prepare students to be accountable leaders who will bring to their work a grasp of complexity, effective problem-solving and communication skills, and an enduring commitment to learning and ethical conduct. Members of the University of Vermont community embrace and advance the values of Our Common Ground: Respect, Integrity, Innovation, Openness, Justice, and Responsibility. Staff play a critical role in this effort and the successful candidate will demonstrate a strong commitment to UVM’s mission and advancing Our Common Ground values through the execution of their job duties. Position Information Position Title Business Operations OC2 N Posting Number S6359PO Department Psychiatry/55750 Position Number 005872 Percent of Full-Time 1.00 Standard Hours at 1.0 FTE 37.5 Term (months per year) 12 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Chronicle of Higher Education HigherEdJobs Inside Higher Ed LinkedIn Seven Days UVM Employee (Please specify below) UVM Employment Web Site Vermont JobLink (Department of Labor) Other (Please specify below) Please specify here where applicable. Enter \"NA\" if not applicable. (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application Optional Documents ©2019 The University of Vermont – Burlington, VT 05405 – (802) 656-3131 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be los