    "https://www.uvmjobs.com/postings/88551": {
      "title": "Laboratory Research Technician",
      "description": "University of Vermont Employment Opportunities | Laboratory Research Technician Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UVM Employee Wellness Human Resources UVM Cultural Resource Guide FAQ Clery Act Reports Laboratory Research Technician Please carefully review the details of this position below. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job button (or see the Special Instructions below if no button appears). If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark button. The University of Vermont is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, or any other category legally protected by federal or state law. For information on safety and security at the University of Vermont, see the annual security report by clicking on the Clery Act button in the sidebar menu. Finalists for positions at UVM may be subject to a criminal background check. For classified staff positions, actual hiring pay dependent on current competitor market conditions, comparable campus peer(s) at time of hire, and candidate’s experience level and length. Be sure to carefully review and update your application information before submitting an application! Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Details Advertising/Posting Title Laboratory Research Technician Posting Summary The Laboratory Research Technician will provide technical and operational support to a laboratory studying the molecular basis of autoimmune disease using mouse models. Perform established molecular biology, immunology, animal, and cell culture procedures according to laboratory protocols. Collect, organize, and maintain experimental data and laboratory records. Assist with animal colony maintenance and routine laboratory operations. Minimum Qualifications (or equivalent combination of education and experience) Bachelor’s degree in Biology, Microbiology, Biochemistry, or related field, or equivalent combination of education and experience. Basic knowledge of biological laboratory methods. Ability to learn and follow established laboratory procedures and maintain accurate records. Effective organizational and communication skills and proficiency with standard computer applications. Desirable Qualifications Experience with molecular biology, immunology, cell culture, and/or laboratory rodents. Anticipated Pay Range $22.00- $27.00 Other Information Special Conditions A probationary period may be required, Contingent on continued funding, Occasional evening and/or weekends required (if non-exempt position, may result in overtime), Background Check required for this position FLSA Non-Exempt Union Position Yes, UVMSU Posting Details Position will be posted for a minimum of one week, after which it is subject to removal without notice. Job Location Burlington, Vermont, United States Job Open Date 10/14/2026 Job Close Date (Jobs close at 11:59 PM EST.) Open Until Filled No Our Common Ground Statement The University of Vermont is a welcoming, educationally purposeful community committed to creating an inclusive environment that embraces intellectual diversity and global perspectives. We seek to prepare students to be accountable leaders who will bring to their work a grasp of complexity, effective problem-solving and communication skills, and an enduring commitment to learning and ethical conduct. Members of the University of Vermont community embrace and advance the values of Our Common Ground: Respect, Integrity, Innovation, Openness, Justice, and Responsibility. Staff play a critical role in this effort and the successful candidate will demonstrate a strong commitment to UVM’s mission and advancing Our Common Ground values through the execution of their job duties. Position Information Position Title Research Laboratory OC2 N Posting Number S6355PO Department Biomedical and Health Sci/56030 Position Number 00023310 Percent of Full-Time 1.0 Standard Hours at 1.0 FTE 37.5 Term (months per year) 12 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application Optional Documents ©2019 The University of Vermont – Burlington, VT 05405 – (802) 656-3131 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
