    "https://www.uvmjobs.com/postings/88526": {
      "title": "Deputy Chief Financial Officer",
      "description": "University of Vermont Employment Opportunities | Deputy Chief Financial Officer Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UVM Employee Wellness Human Resources UVM Cultural Resource Guide FAQ Clery Act Reports Deputy Chief Financial Officer Please carefully review the details of this position below. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job button (or see the Special Instructions below if no button appears). If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark button. The University of Vermont is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, or any other category legally protected by federal or state law. For information on safety and security at the University of Vermont, see the annual security report by clicking on the Clery Act button in the sidebar menu. Finalists for positions at UVM may be subject to a criminal background check. For classified staff positions, actual hiring pay dependent on current competitor market conditions, comparable campus peer(s) at time of hire, and candidate’s experience level and length. Be sure to carefully review and update your application information before submitting an application! Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Details Advertising/Posting Title Deputy Chief Financial Officer Posting Summary The Deputy Chief Financial Officer (Deputy CFO ) serves as a senior leader within the Division of Finance and Administration and reports directly to the Senior Vice President for Finance and Administration. The Deputy CFO serves as the principal deputy and strategic partner to the Senior Vice President and assists in providing leadership, oversight, and direction for the University’s financial planning, budgeting, financial analysis, operational effectiveness, and long-term financial sustainability. Working closely with academic and administrative leaders, the Deputy CFO advances institutional priorities through strategic financial leadership, data-informed decision-making, resource planning, and continuous improvement. The position plays a critical role in evaluating institutional opportunities and risks, supporting executive decision-making, and ensuring the effective stewardship of University resources. The Deputy CFO combines executive financial leadership with a strong focus on financial strategy, innovation, organizational effectiveness, and business transformation. The position operates with a high degree of independence and judgment and may represent or act on behalf of the Senior Vice President in designated matters. The Deputy CFO helps shape institutional financial strategy and supports the long-term health and viability of the University. Minimum Qualifications (or equivalent combination of education and experience) Master’s degree in Finance, Accounting, Business Administration, Economics, Public Administration, Higher Education Administration, or a related field. Eight years of progressively responsible leadership experience in finance, budgeting, financial planning and analysis, accounting, business operations, administration, or a related field. Demonstrated leadership experience in higher education. Demonstrated experience leading complex financial planning, budgeting, forecasting, strategic finance, or institutional analysis initiatives. Experience with higher education budget models, IBB , capital planning, debt management, treasury operations, or enterprise financial strategy. Demonstrated experience developing and applying advanced financial models and analytical frameworks to support executive decision-making. Experience leading cross-functional initiatives and influencing organizational decision making in a complex environment. Experience supervising professional staff and organizational units. Strong analytical, problem-solving, communication, and presentation skills. Demonstrated ability to build effective partnerships across diverse stakeholder groups. Desirable Qualifications Experience supporting executive leadership teams, governing boards, and institutional strategic planning efforts. Demonstrated experience leading operational improvement, business transformation, ERP modernization, or organizational change initiatives. Anticipated Pay Range $175,000 to $225,000 Other Information Special Conditions A probationary period may be required, Background Check required for this position FLSA Exempt Union Position No Posting Details Position will be posted for a minimum of one week, after which it is subject to removal without notice. Job Location Burlington, Vermont, United States Job Open Date 10/12/2026 Job Close Date (Jobs close at 11:59 PM EST.) Open Until Filled No Our Common Ground Statement The University of Vermont is a welcoming, educationally purposeful community committed to creating an inclusive environment that embraces intellectual diversity and global perspectives. We seek to prepare students to be accountable leaders who will bring to their work a grasp of complexity, effective problem-solving and communication skills, and an enduring commitment to learning and ethical conduct. Members of the University of Vermont community embrace and advance the values of Our Common Ground: Respect, Integrity, Innovation, Openness, Justice, and Responsibility. Staff play a critical role in this effort and the successful candidate will demonstrate a strong commitment to UVM’s mission and advancing Our Common Ground values through the execution of their job duties. Position Information Position Title Fiscal Ops & Bus Mgmt PC5 X Posting Number S6348PO Department VP Finance & Administration/11000 Position Number 00028016 Percent of Full-Time 1.0 Standard Hours at 1.0 FTE 37.5 Term (months per year) 12 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application Optional Documents ©2019 The University of Vermont – Burlington, VT 05405 – (802) 656-3131 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
