state, and foundation grants financial and activity reporting requirements, assist with budget development and creation of funding proposals in UVMClick for grant applications, and facilitate processes related to personnel management (new hires, effort certification, and salary distributions). Serve as the point person for the OPC and AHEC on PeopleSoft matters, facilities and space, and technology/ COMTS matters. Coordinate complex, multidisciplinary health workforce and medical education initiatives, in partnership with Program Director and AHEC faculty. This includes contributing to the development of project processes and documentation, supporting recruitment and enrollment into programs, tracking grant-required deliverables and program timeline, funder reporting, and stakeholder engagement. Collaborate with office leadership and grant principal investigators. Work closely with the UVM Sponsored Project Administration ( SPA ), Accounting and Procurement Services, and the regional AHECs. The position reports to OPC / AHEC Program Director. Minimum Qualifications (or equivalent combination of education and experience) Bachelor’s degree and two to four years of related experience required or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Effective financial management and communication skills. Ability to effectively respond to a wide variety of individuals and their varying needs including UVM , the regional AHECs, and the public. Demonstrated ability to attend to detail. Effective time-management skills and ability to prioritize effectively to meet deadlines; Ability to manage multiple projects simultaneously. Ability to take initiative and ability to work independently as well as collaboratively within a team. Ability to use discretion regarding disclosure/dissemination/security of confidential/sensitive information. Proficiency in Microsoft Word, Excel, Teams, and Outlook is essential. A commitment to continuous quality and process improvement. Desirable Qualifications Experience in higher education and grant-funded organizations highly desirable. PMP certification. Knowledge of Microsoft Access, Sharepoint, project management software, Concur, PeopleSoft, UVM financial systems, and fund accounting are highly desirable. An understanding of education financing/student loan programs. Anticipated Pay Range $60000 - $70000 Other Information Position is partially funded by grants Special Conditions A probationary period may be required, Contingent on continued funding, This position is eligible for a hybrid schedule with an option to split time between campus and elsewhere, in accordance with the university telecommuting policy, Background Check required for this position FLSA Exempt Union Position Yes, UVMSU Posting Details Position will be posted for a minimum of one week, after which it is subject to removal without notice. Job Location Burlington, Vermont, United States Job Open Date 09/29/2026 Job Close Date (Jobs close at 11:59 PM EST.) Open Until Filled Yes Our Common Ground Statement The University of Vermont is a welcoming, educationally purposeful community committed to creating an inclusive environment that embraces intellectual diversity and global perspectives. We seek to prepare students to be accountable leaders who will bring to their work a grasp of complexity, effective problem-solving and communication skills, and an enduring commitment to learning and ethical conduct. Members of the University of Vermont community embrace and advance the values of Our Common Ground: Respect, Integrity, Innovation, Openness, Justice, and Responsibility. Staff play a critical role in this effort and the successful candidate will demonstrate a strong commitment to UVM’s mission and advancing Our Common Ground values through the execution of their job duties. Position Information Position Title Business Operations PC2 X Posting Number S6329PO Department COM Ofc of Primary Care/55022 Position Number 00028010 Percent of Full-Time 1.0 Standard Hours at 1.0 FTE 37.5 Term (months per year) 12 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Chronicle of Higher Education HigherEdJobs Inside Higher Ed LinkedIn Seven Days UVM Employee (Please specify below) UVM Employment Web Site Vermont JobLink (Department of Labor) Other (Please specify below) * Please specify here where applicable. Enter \"NA\" if not applicable. (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application Optional Documents ©2019 The University of Vermont – Burlington, VT 05405 – (802) 656-3131 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
