    "https://www.uvmjobs.com/postings/88466": {
      "title": "Catamount Educational Farm Production Coordinator",
      "description": "University of Vermont Employment Opportunities | Catamount Educational Farm Production Coordinator Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UVM Employee Wellness Human Resources UVM Cultural Resource Guide FAQ Clery Act Reports Catamount Educational Farm Production Coordinator Please carefully review the details of this position below. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job button (or see the Special Instructions below if no button appears). If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark button. The University of Vermont is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, or any other category legally protected by federal or state law. For information on safety and security at the University of Vermont, see the annual security report by clicking on the Clery Act button in the sidebar menu. Finalists for positions at UVM may be subject to a criminal background check. For classified staff positions, actual hiring pay dependent on current competitor market conditions, comparable campus peer(s) at time of hire, and candidate’s experience level and length. Be sure to carefully review and update your application information before submitting an application! Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Details Advertising/Posting Title Catamount Educational Farm Production Coordinator Posting Summary The Catamount Educational Farm Production Coordinator will provide management of vegetable production in support of on-farm educational programming. Develop and implement an overall farm plan in support of College of Agriculture and Life Science ( CALS ) undergraduate programs; Community Supported Agriculture ( CSA ), farm stand, and institutional produce sales. Support faculty with classroom and field instruction for Agriculture, Landscape, and Environment ( ALE ) and related courses, as well as other programs held on site. Assist on-farm researchers with plot preparation and experiment implementation. Minimum Qualifications (or equivalent combination of education and experience) Bachelor’s Degree in plant science or related field and minimum three years of experience in vegetable farm management and education. Thorough understanding of diversified agriculture systems used in Vermont and the surrounding region. Effective analytical, communication, organizational and teaching skills. Working knowledge of applicable food safety, farm safety, and regulatory programs that apply to agricultural systems. Valid driver’s license required to operate farm vehicles. Ability and experience to safely and efficiently operate farm equipment. Vermont Pesticide applicator license or the ability to obtain prior to the first growing season required. Desirable Qualifications Master’s Degree in plant science or related field. Experience teaching in a hands-on environment, and or, college teaching experience. Experience in curriculum development for undergraduate and / or adult learners. Knowledge of operational budgets for farm systems. Anticipated Pay Range $42,400 - 48,800 (0.8FTE) Other Information This position is being hired at a .80 FTE , but could increase to 1.0 FTE , based on the incumbent’s experience and ability to help grow the farm operations. At a .80 FTE , there may also be potential for qualified individuals to teach up to one three-credit course per semester as a part-time lecturer, in accordance with the UVM Staff Teaching Policy. Position located in the Horticulture Research and Education Center in South Burlington, VT. Special Conditions A probationary period may be required, Contingent on continued funding, Occasional evening and/or weekends required (if non-exempt position, may result in overtime), Background Check required for this position, A post-offer pre-employment (POPE test) physical examination is required FLSA Exempt Union Position Yes, UVMSU Posting Details Position will be posted for a minimum of one week, after which it is subject to removal without notice. Job Location South Burlington, Vermont, United States Job Open Date 10/08/2026 Job Close Date (Jobs close at 11:59 PM EST.) Open Until Filled No Our Common Ground Statement The University of Vermont is a welcoming, educationally purposeful community committed to creating an inclusive environment that embraces intellectual diversity and global perspectives. We seek to prepare students to be accountable leaders who will bring to their work a grasp of complexity, effective problem-solving and communication skills, and an enduring commitment to learning and ethical conduct. Members of the University of Vermont community embrace and advance the values of Our Common Ground: Respect, Integrity, Innovation, Openness, Justice, and Responsibility. Staff play a critical role in this effort and the successful candidate will demonstrate a strong commitment to UVM’s mission and advancing Our Common Ground values through the execution of their job duties. Position Information Position Title Outreach Education PC2 X Posting Number S6340PO Department Plant & Animal Biology Fclty/51060 Position Number 00025464 Percent of Full-Time 0.80 Standard Hours at 1.0 FTE 37.5 Term (months per year) 12 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please specify here where applicable. Enter \"NA\" if not applicable. (Open Ended Question) * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Chronicle of Higher Education HigherEdJobs Inside Higher Ed LinkedIn Seven Days UVM Employee (Please specify below) UVM Employment Web Site Vermont JobLink (Department of Labor) Other (Please specify below) Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of