    "https://www.uvmjobs.com/postings/88460": {
      "title": "PACE Deputy Chief Officer",
      "description": "University of Vermont Employment Opportunities | PACE Deputy Chief Officer Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UVM Employee Wellness Human Resources UVM Cultural Resource Guide FAQ Clery Act Reports PACE Deputy Chief Officer Please carefully review the details of this position below. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job button (or see the Special Instructions below if no button appears). If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark button. The University of Vermont is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, or any other category legally protected by federal or state law. For information on safety and security at the University of Vermont, see the annual security report by clicking on the Clery Act button in the sidebar menu. Finalists for positions at UVM may be subject to a criminal background check. For classified staff positions, actual hiring pay dependent on current competitor market conditions, comparable campus peer(s) at time of hire, and candidate’s experience level and length. Be sure to carefully review and update your application information before submitting an application! Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Details Advertising/Posting Title PACE Deputy Chief Officer Posting Summary Deputy PACE Chief Officer Professional and Continuing Education ( PACE ) | University of Vermont Are you a visionary leader who thrives at the intersection of strategy, innovation, and operational excellence? Join the University of Vermont’s Professional and Continuing Education ( PACE ) team as the Deputy PACE Chief Officer, a pivotal leadership role responsible for driving organizational performance, advancing online education, and shaping the future of lifelong learning. Working closely with the Chief Officer for PACE , you will provide strategic and operational leadership across the organization’s diverse portfolio. With broad oversight of key functional areas, you will ensure programs, services, and processes are aligned to institutional priorities, positioned for growth, and supported to achieve ambitious performance goals. What You’ll Lead Strategic and operational oversight of online education, program development, enrollment management, student services, program portfolio management, and academic innovation. Implementation of the UVM Online Roadmap and advancement of innovative learning initiatives that support enrollment growth, student success, academic quality, accessibility, workforce relevance, and expanded educational access. Development of sustainable infrastructure, policies, processes, partnerships, and service models that strengthen online and continuing education offerings. Strategic program planning, market research, enrollment forecasting, program evaluation, and assessment in collaboration with academic units. What You’ll Influence As a senior leader, you will collaborate with faculty, academic and administrative leaders, employers, technology teams, and external partners to advance PACE’s mission and strategic priorities. You will represent the Chief Officer in key forums, help guide critical organizational decisions, and play an integral role on the PACE Senior Management Team in evaluating progress toward strategic goals and future opportunities. Why This Role Matters This is more than an operations leadership position. It is an opportunity to help define the future of professional, online, and continuing education at UVM . You will lead transformational initiatives, build cross-campus partnerships, and create innovative pathways that expand access and opportunity for learners throughout Vermont and beyond. Join us in advancing educational innovation, supporting learner success, and shaping the future of higher education. Minimum Qualifications (or equivalent combination of education and experience) Master’s degree in related field and 7–10 years of academic operations, curricular development/design, and online education leadership experience in higher education required. Experience designing end-to-end online infrastructure. Experience in online teaching and instructional design. Demonstrated success leading organizational transformation. Solid leadership, project management, supervisory, market research, organizational and communications skills necessary. Demonstrated understanding of statistical/enrollment trends. Knowledge of higher education philosophy, governance, structure and culture. Strong understanding of financial models and budget expectations. Desirable Qualifications Doctorate Degree. Experience scaling online programs across multiple units. Knowledge of regulatory requirements for online education. Experience linking online strategy to enrollment growth. Anticipated Pay Range $129,000 to $170,000 Other Information Special Conditions A probationary period may be required, Occasional evening and/or weekends required (if non-exempt position, may result in overtime), This position is eligible for a hybrid schedule with an option to split time between campus and elsewhere, in accordance with the university telecommuting policy, Background Check required for this position FLSA Exempt Union Position No Posting Details Position will be posted for a minimum of one week, after which it is subject to removal without notice. Job Location Burlington, Vermont, United States Job Open Date 10/01/2026 Job Close Date (Jobs close at 11:59 PM EST.) Open Until Filled No Our Common Ground Statement The University of Vermont is a welcoming, educationally purposeful community committed to creating an inclusive environment that embraces intellectual diversity and global perspectives. We seek to prepare students to be accountable leaders who will bring to their work a grasp of complexity, effective problem-solving and communication skills, and an enduring commitment to learning and ethical conduct. Members of the University of Vermont community embrace and advance the values of Our Common Ground: Respect, Integrity, Innovation, Openness, Justice, and Responsibility. Staff play a critical role in this effort and the successful candidate will demonstrate a strong commitment to UVM’s mission and advancing Our Common Ground values through the execution of their job duties. Position Information Position Title Academic Prgm Mgmt MG4 X Posting Number S6333PO Department PACE - Administration/50100 Position Number 001052 Percent of Full-Time 1.0 Standard Hours at 1.0 FTE 37.5 Term (months per year) 12 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Chronicle of Higher Education HigherEdJobs Inside Higher Ed LinkedIn Seven Days UVM Employee (Please specify below) UVM Employment Web Site Vermont JobLink (Department of Labor) Other (Please specify below) * Please specify here where applicable. Enter \"NA\" if not applicable. (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application Optional Documents ©2019 The University of Vermont – Burlington, VT 05405 – (802) 656-3131 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
