      "title": "CAS HR &amp; Faculty Actions Specialist",
      "description": "University of Vermont Employment Opportunities | CAS HR &amp; Faculty Actions Specialist Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UVM Employee Wellness Human Resources UVM Cultural Resource Guide FAQ Clery Act Reports CAS HR & Faculty Actions Specialist Please carefully review the details of this position below. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job button (or see the Special Instructions below if no button appears). If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark button. The University of Vermont is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, or any other category legally protected by federal or state law. For information on safety and security at the University of Vermont, see the annual security report by clicking on the Clery Act button in the sidebar menu. Finalists for positions at UVM may be subject to a criminal background check. For classified staff positions, actual hiring pay dependent on current competitor market conditions, comparable campus peer(s) at time of hire, and candidate’s experience level and length. Be sure to carefully review and update your application information before submitting an application! Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Details Advertising/Posting Title CAS HR & Faculty Actions Specialist Posting Summary The CAS HR/Fac Actions Specialist will coordinate and support specialized human resources and administrative functions for academic departments within the College of Arts and Sciences, College Administrative Services ( CAS – CAS ). Provide administrative and procedural support for faculty actions, including reappointment, promotion and tenure ( RPT ), and sabbatical leave; support Schedule of Courses planning and development; and assist with faculty and staff recruitment, hiring, and other personnel activities. Interpret and communicate university policies, procedures, and applicable collective bargaining agreements, providing guidance to faculty, department administrators, and academic leaders while collaborating with campus partners to ensure the accurate and timely processing of actions. As part of a collaborative team supporting a cooperative model, serve as a primary point of contact for inquiries, facilitate clear and consistent communication, coordinate workflows, maintain records, and assist in resolving procedural issues. Monitor processes, identify opportunities for improvement, and ensure compliance with department, college, university, and collective bargaining agreement requirements. Minimum Qualifications (or equivalent combination of education and experience) Bachelor’s degree in human resources, business administration, or related field and two to four years of related experience in an administrative setting required. Proficiency with Microsoft Office applications, (especially Excel, Word), and database applications required, and familiarity with internet resources required. Effective analytical, problem solving, organizational, communication, interpersonal, team-collaboration, and writing skills required. Attention to detail and accuracy required. Demonstrated experience and commitment to overall customer service and ability to discern and maintain confidential information required. Desirable Qualifications Experience using human resource and enrollment/student management systems, such as PeopleSoft, PeopleAdmin, and Banner highly desirable. Anticipated Pay Range $27.50 - $28.97/hour Other Information Applicants are asked to apply online. Please provide a cover letter, resume and contact information for three professional references. The College of Arts and Sciences ( CAS ) at the University of Vermont welcomes difference, values collaboration, encourages debate, and stands for integrity, service, and academic excellence. We are dedicated to the rigorous pursuit, understanding, and dissemination of knowledge through the process of discovery, the creation of art, and the practice of teaching. We provide an integrated and engaging multidisciplinary experience that generates creativity, critical thought, effective communication, and a practiced commitment to serve the pressing needs of society and the natural world. For more information about the College of Arts & Sciences ( CAS ), please visit the CAS website, www.uvm.edu/cas . Special Conditions A probationary period may be required, Background Check required for this position FLSA Non-Exempt Union Position No Posting Details Position will be posted for a minimum of one week, after which it is subject to removal without notice. Job Location Burlington, Vermont, United States Job Open Date 09/22/2026 Job Close Date (Jobs close at 11:59 PM EST.) Open Until Filled No Our Common Ground Statement The University of Vermont is a welcoming, educationally purposeful community committed to creating an inclusive environment that embraces intellectual diversity and global perspectives. We seek to prepare students to be accountable leaders who will bring to their work a grasp of complexity, effective problem-solving and communication skills, and an enduring commitment to learning and ethical conduct. Members of the University of Vermont community embrace and advance the values of Our Common Ground: Respect, Integrity, Innovation, Openness, Justice, and Responsibility. Staff play a critical role in this effort and the successful candidate will demonstrate a strong commitment to UVM’s mission and advancing Our Common Ground values through the execution of their job duties. Position Information Position Title Business Operations OC2 N Posting Number S6316PO Department CAS College Admin Services/52360 Position Number 00026806 Percent of Full-Time 1.0 Standard Hours at 1.0 FTE 37.5 Term (months per year) 12 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application Optional Documents Other Document (1) Other Document (2) Other Document (3) Other Document (4) Other Document (5) ©2019 The University of Vermont – Burlington, VT 05405 – (802) 656-3131 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.uvmjobs.com/postings/88454": {
      "title": "Technical Support Specialist",
      "description": "University of Vermont Employment Opportunities | Technical Support Specialist Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UVM Employee Wellness Human Resources UVM Cultural Resource Guide FAQ Clery Act Reports Technical Support Specialist Please carefully review the details of this position below. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job button (or see the Special Instructions below if no button appears). If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark button. The University of Vermont is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, or any other category legally protected by federal or state law. For information on safety and security at the University of Vermont, see the annual security report by clicking on the Clery Act button in the sidebar menu. Finalists for positions at UVM may be subject to a criminal background check. For classified staff positions, actual hiring pay dependent on current competitor market conditions, comparable campus peer(s) at time of hire, and candidate’s experience level and length. Be sure to carefully review and update your application information before submitting an application! Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Details Advertising/Posting Title Technical Support Specialist Posting Summary The Technical Support Specialist will provide technical, administrative, and customer service support for the University’s access control, CATcard, and safety technology systems. As a member of the Department of Safety Technology & Training team, this position helps support the technologies and services that keep campus facilities secure, accessible, and operating effectively for students, faculty, staff, and visitors. Responsibilities include managing access permissions and schedules, troubleshooting software and system issues, supporting technology projects and system upgrades, maintaining equipment and operational records, and assisting customers through a variety of service channels. The successful candidate will work closely with team members, campus departments, and technology partners while developing technical expertise, contributing to campus-wide initiatives, and supporting systems that have a visible impact across the University community. Minimum Qualifications (or equivalent combination of education and experience) Associate’s degree and one to three years of related experience required, or an equivalent combination of education, training, and experience. Demonstrated ability to provide excellent customer service, maintain accurate records, and perform administrative or technical support functions required. Strong communication, interpersonal, problem-solving, and organizational skills required. Ability to manage multiple priorities, work independently, and effectively support a diverse customer population required. Proficiency with computer systems and standard business software applications required. Valid driver’s license and successful driver’s check required. Desirable Qualifications Experience providing customer service, technical support, training, or administrative support. Strong technical aptitude and the ability to quickly learn new software applications and systems. Proficiency with Microsoft Office applications, including Word, Excel, Outlook, and Teams. Familiarity with databases, recordkeeping systems, higher education environments, access management, or security-related technologies is desirable but not required. Anticipated Pay Range $25.64-$28.21 Other Information May need to serve on call outside of standard business hours. Special Conditions A probationary period may be required, This position is ineligible for telework due to the essential functions, Background Check required for this position FLSA Non-Exempt Union Position Yes, UVMSU Posting Details Position will be posted for a minimum of one week, after which it is subject to removal without notice. Job Location Burlington, Vermont, United States Job Open Date 10/07/2026 Job Close Date (Jobs close at 11:59 PM EST.) Open Until Filled Yes Our Common Ground Statement The University of Vermont is a welcoming, educationally purposeful community committed to creating an inclusive environment that embraces intellectual diversity and global perspectives. We seek to prepare students to be accountable leaders who will bring to their work a grasp of complexity, effective problem-solving and communication skills, and an enduring commitment to learning and ethical conduct. Members of the University of Vermont community embrace and advance the values of Our Common Ground: Respect, Integrity, Innovation, Openness, Justice, and Responsibility. Staff play a critical role in this effort and the successful candidate will demonstrate a strong commitment to UVM’s mission and advancing Our Common Ground values through the execution of their job duties. Position Information Position Title Technology Support OC3 N Posting Number S6338PO Department CatCard Service Center/11565 Position Number 010580 Percent of Full-Time 1.00 Standard Hours at 1.0 FTE 37.5 Term (months per year) 12 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please specify here where applicable. Enter \"NA\" if not applicable. (Open Ended Question) * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Chronicle of Higher Education HigherEdJobs Inside Higher Ed LinkedIn Seven Days UVM Employee (Please specify below) UVM Employment Web Site Vermont JobLink (Department of Labor) Other (Please specify below) Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application Optional Documents ©2019 The University of Vermont – Burlington, VT 05405 – (802) 656-3131 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
