 Coordinate and set up meetings, including scheduling, room reservations, technology needs, agendas, materials, records, and follow-up tracking. Support Dean’s Office leadership and Dean’s Office initiatives with administrative projects by organizing information, maintaining accurate files, and escalating issues that require leadership attention. Consistently exercise discretion and sound judgment when handling sensitive, confidential, and time-critical information and communications. Minimum Qualifications (or equivalent combination of education and experience) Associate’s degree in a related field and five (5) years of related experience, or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Working knowledge of software applications used to support administrative operations and familiarity with internet resources and proficiency with Microsoft Office (Word, Excel, Outlook, Teams) required. Demonstrated ability to coordinate multiple activities with attention to detail, meet deadlines, and maintain accurate records. Effective interpersonal, organizational, and written communication skills required. Demonstrated ability to exercise discretion and maintain confidentiality when working with sensitive information. Desirable Qualifications Experience providing executive-level administrative support in a complex office environment. Experience coordinating sensitive calendars, preparing briefing materials, managing confidential communications, tracking decisions and follow-up items. Familiarity with university processes. Anticipated Pay Range $26.50-$34.00/hr Other Information Final compensation will be determined in consideration of the finalist’s experience.. Special Conditions A probationary period may be required, Occasional evening and/or weekends required (if non-exempt position, may result in overtime), This position is ineligible for telework due to the essential functions, Background Check required for this position FLSA Non-Exempt Union Position No Posting 