    "https://www.uvmjobs.com/postings/88137": {
      "title": "LITERACY EDUCATION - ASSISTANT PROFESSOR (TENURE-TRACK)",
      "description": "University of Vermont Employment Opportunities | LITERACY EDUCATION - ASSISTANT PROFESSOR (TENURE-TRACK) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UVM Employee Wellness Human Resources UVM Cultural Resource Guide FAQ Clery Act Reports LITERACY EDUCATION - ASSISTANT PROFESSOR (TENURE-TRACK) Please carefully review the details of this position below. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job button (or see the Special Instructions below if no button appears). If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark button. The University of Vermont is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, or any other category legally protected by federal or state law. For information on safety and security at the University of Vermont, see the annual security report by clicking on the Clery Act button in the sidebar menu. Finalists for positions at UVM may be subject to a criminal background check. For classified staff positions, actual hiring pay dependent on current competitor market conditions, comparable campus peer(s) at time of hire, and candidate’s experience level and length. Be sure to carefully review and update your application information before submitting an application! Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Posting Details Position will be posted for a minimum of one week, after which it is subject to removal without notice. Advertising Copy The College of Education and Social Services ( CESS ) at the University of Vermont invites nominations and applications for a full-time, nine-month, tenure-track position in the Department of Education beginning Fall 2027, at the rank of Assistant Professor with research and teaching that emphasize foundational literacy or literacy development in early ages/grades. Applicants should be motivated by the opportunity to contribute to the CESS mission to \"create a more humane and just society.” The successful candidate will demonstrate expertise in foundational literacy through publications, teaching, and service. We are particularly interested in those with training in quantitative methods and experience with grant-writing and oversight of externally funded projects. The University Established in 1791, the University of Vermont is classified as a prestigious Carnegie R1 institution and consistently ranked as one of the top public universities in the United States. UVM is distinctive for its small New-England liberal arts college feel. UVM’s tradition of equity and social justice extends not only to faculty, staff, and students, but also is reflected in a commitment to environmentally sound and sustainable practices. Notable innovations include complex data mapping and analysis, material innovation, social and rural health and mental health, and health and medical sciences. The College The Mission of The College of Education and Social Services is to educate and prepare outstanding professionals in education, human services, and social work; engage in scholarship of high quality; and provide exemplary professional service to Vermont, the nation, and the world. We do this to contribute to a more humane and just society, free from oppression, that maximizes human potential and the quality of life for all individuals, families and communities. The Department The Department of Education is home to educator and leadership preparation programs at the UG, Masters, EdD and PhD levels, with graduate programs ranked # 69 by USNWR . The programs are nationally accredited, award recognized, and known for high-impact instructional practices with a community-engagement focus. Faculty are nationally and internationally recognized in their fields as evidenced by disciplinary awards, Fullbright and Spencer awards, and comparative faculty metrics placing us in the top tiers of publications and interdisciplinary scholarly works. The Community Burlington, Vermont, is ranked by Indeed as the #3 best city to work in the United States and CNN ranks Burlington as #6 as “America’s Best Towns to Visit in 2026.” Burlington and UVM share a panoramic setting on the shores of Lake Champlain, between the Green Mountains of Vermont and the Adirondack Mountains of New York State. We are a walkable and bikeable community with University sponsored ride sharing and public transportation. The Burlington International Airport is served by Delta, American, United and other major carriers. We have a rich cultural, civic, and arts community as well as a wide range of outdoor activities year-round. Vermont’s size and history support an environment of access and opportunities for collaborative agency partnerships throughout the state and region. Responsibilities: The successful candidate will assume a range of responsibilities that include: Consistent and cohesive program of research Excellence in teaching and advising Collegial service contributions Required Qualifications: Doctoral degree in a relevant discipline Record of publication commensurate with rank Relevant experience with external grant funding Teaching excellence in higher education Strong collegial, communication, and collaborative teamwork skills Preferred Qualifications: Foundational literacy expertise relevant for educator preparation programs Collaborative skills and experience with state department policies and literacy-related change initiatives related to literacy Content area expertise in literacy interventions across universal instruction and tier 2 and 3 interventions Experience and commitment that will help elevate UVM’s position as a leader in literacy in the state and beyond The University of Vermont is a welcoming, educationally purposeful community committed to creating an inclusive environment that embraces intellectual diversity and global perspectives. We seek to prepare students to be accountable leaders who will bring to their work a grasp of complexity, effective problem-solving and communication skills, and an enduring commitment to learning and ethical conduct. Members of the University of Vermont community embrace and advance the values of Our Common Ground : Respect, Integrity, Innovation, Openness, Justice, and Responsibility. The successful candidate will demonstrate a strong commitment to UVM’s mission and advancing Our Common Ground values through their teaching, service, research, scholarship, or creative arts. Salary Range (9 Mo) : Assistant Professor: $79,000-$82,000 Final offers include a start-up package for research, with salary determinations based upon experience and qualifications. Application Process Review of applications will begin October 15, 2026, and continue until the position is filled. For more detailed information about us, visit our web pages Department of Education ; the College of Education and Social Services ; and the University of Vermont. . Anticipated starting date is August 23, 2027 . Please apply online at www.uvmjobs.com . Include 1) a cover letter specifically addressing how your qualifications meet position requirements; 2) a current curriculum vitae; 3) a separate 1 page statement on how you, as a faculty member in the department, would enhance the impact of Our Common Ground Values at UVM ; and 4) the names and email addresses of three references who can be contacted for letters of support before a candidate is advanced to on-campus interviews in the search process. For all applicants, employment is subject to a successful background check. For more information about the position, please contact the Search Committee Chair, Lori Meyer, at lori.meyer@uvm.edu. The University of Vermont is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, or any other category legally protected by federal or state law. Anticipated Pay Range $79,000-$82,000 Final offers include a start-up package for research, with salary determinations based upon experience and qualifications. Job Location Burlington, Vermont, United States Job Open Date 09/16/2026 Job Close Date Category Position Information Posting Number F3763PO Department Education/53010 Advertising/Posting Title LITERACY EDUCATION - ASSISTANT PROFESSOR (TENURE-TRACK) FLSA Exempt Position Number 00020661 Employee FTE 1.00 Employee Term (months) 9 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Curriculum Vitae Other Document (1) Optional Documents Other Document (2) ©2019 The University of Vermont – Burlington, VT 05405 – (802) 656-3131 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.uvmjobs.com/postings/88109": {
      "title": "Assistant Dean for Finance &amp; Administration",
      "description": "University of Vermont Employment Opportunities | Assistant Dean for Finance &amp; Administration Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UVM Employee Wellness Human Resources UVM Cultural Resource Guide FAQ Clery Act Reports Assistant Dean for Finance & Administration Please carefully review the details of this position below. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job button (or see the Special Instructions below if no button appears). If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark button. The University of Vermont is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, or any other category legally protected by federal or state law. For information on safety and security at the University of Vermont, see the annual security report by clicking on the Clery Act button in the sidebar menu. Finalists for positions at UVM may be subject to a criminal background check. For classified staff positions, actual hiring pay dependent on current competitor market conditions, comparable campus peer(s) at time of hire, and candidate’s experience level and length. Be sure to carefully review and update your application information before submitting an application! Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Details Advertising/Posting Title Assistant Dean for Finance & Administration Posting Summary The Assistant Dean for Finance & Administration is responsible for all complex administrative functions and business operations within the College of Education and Social Services ( CESS ). The Assistant Dean acts as the chief financial manager and the chief human resource manager for the College, accountable for directing and managing financial, budget planning, administrative, human resources, technology, space planning, and business management activities to support the College’s Strategic Alignment Plan ( SAP ), UVM’s Green, Gold, and Bold strategic plan, and values of Our Common Ground. The Assistant Dean is accountable for a team of professional staff managing finance, HR, and operational functions including the Title IVE /Child Welfare Training Partnership Director. The Assistant Dean is a member of the CESS Dean’s Leadership team and reports directly to the Dean. Minimum Qualifications (or equivalent combination of education and experience) Master’s degree in business, financial management, or related field and at least 8 years of experience in financial management, working with large complex budgets, long-range strategic planning, human resources management, business operations, and grants management. Effective analytical, organizational, interpersonal, written and verbal communication skills. Ability to manage competing priorities and meet deadlines. Desirable Qualifications Demonstrated ability to provide consultative leadership Experience in financial decision making that impacts the institution’s mission Supervision of multiple professional positions Higher education administration experience Anticipated Pay Range $125,000-160,000 Other Information Special Conditions A probationary period may be required, Background Check required for this position FLSA Exempt Union Position No Posting Details Position will be posted for a minimum of one week, after which it is subject to removal without notice. Job Location Burlington, Vermont, United States Job Open Date 08/26/2026 Job Close Date (Jobs close at 11:59 PM EST.) Open Until Filled No Our Common Ground Statement The University of Vermont is a welcoming, educationally purposeful community committed to creating an inclusive environment that embraces intellectual diversity and global perspectives. We seek to prepare students to be accountable leaders who will bring to their work a grasp of complexity, effective problem-solving and communication skills, and an enduring commitment to learning and ethical conduct. Members of the University of Vermont community embrace and advance the values of Our Common Ground: Respect, Integrity, Innovation, Openness, Justice, and Responsibility. Staff play a critical role in this effort and the successful candidate will demonstrate a strong commitment to UVM’s mission and advancing Our Common Ground values through the execution of their job duties. Position Information Position Title Business Operations MG4 X Posting Number S6273PO Department CESS Dean's Office/53000 Position Number 007521 Percent of Full-Time 1.0 Standard Hours at 1.0 FTE 37.5 Term (months per year) 12 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application Other Document (1) Optional Documents ©2019 The University of Vermont – Burlington, VT 05405 – (802) 656-3131 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
