    "https://www.uvmjobs.com/postings/80080": {
      "title": "Hematology/Oncology - Assistant/Associate/Full Professor, Clinical Scholar Pathway",
      "description": "University of Vermont Employment Opportunities | Hematology/Oncology - Assistant/Associate/Full Professor, Clinical Scholar Pathway Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UVM Employee Wellness Human Resources UVM Cultural Resource Guide FAQ Clery Act Reports Hematology/Oncology - Assistant/Associate/Full Professor, Clinical Scholar Pathway Please carefully review the details of this position below. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job button (or see the Special Instructions below if no button appears). If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark button. The University of Vermont is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, or any other category legally protected by federal or state law. For information on safety and security at the University of Vermont, see the annual security report by clicking on the Clery Act button in the sidebar menu. Finalists for positions at UVM may be subject to a criminal background check. For classified staff positions, actual hiring pay dependent on current competitor market conditions, comparable campus peer(s) at time of hire, and candidate’s experience level and length. Be sure to carefully review and update your application information before submitting an application! Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Posting Details Position will be posted for a minimum of one week, after which it is subject to removal without notice. Advertising Copy The Division of Hematology/Oncology in the Department of Medicine at the Larner College of Medicine, the University of Vermont Cancer Center and its teaching hospital, the UVM Medical Center and UVM Health Network, is seeking an academic clinician with experience in solid tumor oncology and a focus on breast oncology to join our academic faculty. The position is available at the rank of Assistant/Associate/Full Professor in the Clinical Scholar Pathway. This position involves approximately 80% effort toward clinical oncology care focused on breast cancers with remaining effort protected for scholarly activities. Substantial opportunities exist for collaborative and translational research with investigators in the UVM Cancer Center. Applicants must be ABIM board certified/board eligible in Medical Oncology and must be eligible for medical licensure in the State of Vermont, for privileges at UVM Medical Center, and for faculty appointment at the University of Vermont. Candidates should have a record of or potential for productive cancer-focused clinical research. Burlington is a vibrant community located on the shores of Lake Champlain, between the Adirondack and Green Mountains. With year-round recreational opportunities, safe neighborhoods and excellent schools, this progressive community has been frequently cited as being one of the healthiest and best cities in the US in which to live. The University is especially interested in candidates who can contribute to the diversity and excellence of the academic community through their research, teaching, and/or service. Applicants are requested to include in their cover letter information about how they will further this goal. The University of Vermont is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, or any other category legally protected by federal or state law. The University encourages applications from all individuals who will contribute to the diversity and excellence of the institution. Applicants must apply online at: www.uvmjobs.com under Position No.00024406 (with CV, Cover Letter and three references) . Questions about this opportunity may be directed to: Dr. Randall Holcombe, via email: randall.holcombe@med.uvm.edu . Review of applications will begin immediately. Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Anticipated Pay Range Job Location Burlington, Vermont, United States Job Open Date 07/02/2024 Job Close Date Category Position Information Posting Number F3113PO Department Med-Hematology Oncology/55538 Advertising/Posting Title Hematology/Oncology - Assistant/Associate/Full Professor, Clinical Scholar Pathway FLSA Exempt Position Number 00024406 Employee FTE 1.0 Employee Term (months) 12 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Please specify here where applicable. Enter \"NA\" if not applicable. (Open Ended Question) How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Chronicle of Higher Education HigherEdJobs Inside Higher Ed LinkedIn Seven Days UVM Employee (Please specify below) UVM Employment Web Site Vermont JobLink (Department of Labor) Other (Please specify below) Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter/Letter of Application Optional Documents ©2019 The University of Vermont – Burlington, VT 05405 – (802) 656-3131 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.uvmjobs.com/postings/88734": {
      "title": "AMERICAN SIGN LANGUAGE - LECTURER/SENIOR LECTURER",
      "description": "University of Vermont Employment Opportunities | AMERICAN SIGN LANGUAGE - LECTURER/SENIOR LECTURER Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UVM Employee Wellness Human Resources UVM Cultural Resource Guide FAQ Clery Act Reports AMERICAN SIGN LANGUAGE - LECTURER/SENIOR LECTURER Please carefully review the details of this position below. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job button (or see the Special Instructions below if no button appears). If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark button. The University of Vermont is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, or any other category legally protected by federal or state law. For information on safety and security at the University of Vermont, see the annual security report by clicking on the Clery Act button in the sidebar menu. Finalists for positions at UVM may be subject to a criminal background check. For classified staff positions, actual hiring pay dependent on current competitor market conditions, comparable campus peer(s) at time of hire, and candidate’s experience level and length. Be sure to carefully review and update your application information before submitting an application! Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Posting Details Position will be posted for a minimum of one week, after which it is subject to removal without notice. Advertising Copy The College of Education and Social Services at the University of Vermont invites applications for a full-time, nine-month, non-tenure track position in our American Sign Language ( ASL ) Program beginning in Fall 2027, at the rank of Lecturer/Senior Lecturer. We seek an outstanding instructor in the area of ASL education. Qualified candidates will have experience teaching ASL in postsecondary settings and will work with undergraduate students. We are particularly interested in individuals with a justice-centered approach to pedagogy and language assessment, strong teaching skills, technology savvy, and a record of professional and community services. The University Established in 1791, the University of Vermont is consistently ranked as one of the top public universities in the United States. Our academic programs combine faculty-student relationships most often found in a small liberal arts college with the resources of a major research institution. UVM’s tradition of equity and social justice extends not only to faculty, staff, and students, but also is reflected in a commitment to environmentally sound and sustainable practices. The College The Mission of The College of Education and Social Services is to educate and prepare outstanding professionals in education, human services, and social work; engage in scholarship of high quality; and provide exemplary professional service to Vermont, the nation, and the world. We do this to contribute to a more humane and just society, free from oppression, that maximizes human potential and the quality of life for all individuals, families and communities. The Department The Department of Education is widely recognized for its rigorous academic research, high-quality student experience, innovative teaching practices, and collegial, inclusive work environment. We offer undergraduate and graduate programs in preK – 12 educator preparation, curriculum and instruction, special education, higher education and student affairs, educational leadership and policy studies, and interdisciplinary studies. In addition, we offer undergraduate minors in computer science education, cultural and linguistic diversity, special education, and coaching. The Program The ASL program is designed to help undergraduate students increase their ASL language and cultural competencies and develop a deeper understanding of Deaf experiences through historical, social, and cultural lenses. The curriculum employs an interdisciplinary approach that offers opportunities for students to apply their theoretical knowledge to create an understanding that inspires innovative solutions for problems that perpetuate the marginalization of Deaf people. A combination of ASL competency and cultural knowledge makes students strong candidates for graduate studies or employment in education, communication sciences, and deaf-related fields, as well as more general fields where individuals who are Deaf and hard of hearing are employed. The Community UVM is located in Burlington, Vermont, which is rated as one of the best small cities in the country. The greater Burlington area has an increasingly diverse population of about 125,000 and enjoys a panoramic setting on the shores of Lake Champlain, between the Green Mountains of Vermont and the Adirondack Mountains of New York State. The surrounding area provides an environment rich in cultural, civic, and recreational activities. Vermont has a deep history of social activism and political participation. It offers many opportunities for collaborative partnerships in community and state-wide human service and social change organizations in multiple fields of practice, including state agencies. Responsibilities: The successful candidate at the Lecturer/Senior Lecturer level will assume a range of responsibilities that include: Teaching ASL courses across novice, intermediate, and advanced levels (Lecturers teach 8 courses per year, all are in-person, this is not a remote position); Advising ASL minors Collaborating with the Department of Education faculty and staff in departmental governance and service; Engaging in service activities at the college, university, regional, state, and national levels. Qualifications: Required: Earned Masters in ASL /Deaf-related field or equivalent; Native or near-native fluency in ASL ; Evidence of ASL teaching excellence at the undergraduate level; Commitment to inclusive excellence; Strong knowledge of technological tools that support ASL pedagogy; Knowledge of TRUE+WAY ASL curriculum; Strong collegial, communication, and collaborative teamwork skills. Preferred: Minimum of five years of college-level teaching experience; Strong knowledge of American Sign Language Linguistics and Deaf Culture; Experience using Brightspace for course design and instruction; SALARY RANGE (9 Mo) : Lecturer: $60,200-$63,700 Senior Lecturer: $69,000-$72,500 Salary determinations based upon experience and qualifications. Application Process Review of applications will begin November 16, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. For more detailed information about us, visit our web pages https://www.uvm.edu/cess/doe/faculty-american-sign-language-asl; the College of Education and Social Services’ website ; and the University of Vermont’s website . The University of Vermont is a welcoming, educationally purposeful community committed to creating an inclusive environment that embraces intellectual diversity and global perspectives. We seek to prepare students to be accountable leaders who will bring to their work a grasp of complexity, effective problem-solving and communication skills, and an enduring commitment to learning and ethical conduct. Members of the University of Vermont community embrace and advance the values of Our Common Ground: Respect, Integrity, Innovation, Openness, Justice, and Responsibility. The successful candidate will demonstrate a strong commitment to UVM’s mission and advancing Our Common Ground values through their teaching, service, research, scholarship, or creative arts. Anticipated starting date is August 23, 2027 . Please apply online at www.uvmjobs.com . Include 1) a cover letter specifically addressing how your qualifications meet position requirements; 2) a current curriculum vitae; 3) a separate 1 page statement on how you, as a faculty member in the department, would enhance the impact of Our Common Ground Values at UVM ; and 4) the names and email addresses of three references who can be contacted for letters of support before a candidate is advanced to on-campus interviews in the search process. Candidates that advance to on-campus interviews will also be expected to provide evidence of excellence in teaching. For all applicants, employment is subject to a successful background check. For more information about the position, please contact the Search Committee Chair, Cynthia Reyes at Cynthia.Reyes@uvm.edu. The University of Vermont is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, or any other category legally protected by federal or state law. Anticipated Pay Range Lecturer: $60,200-$63,700 Senior Lecturer: $69,000-$72,500 Salary determinations based upon experience and qualifications. Job Location Burlington, Vermont, United States Job Open Date 10/21/2026 Job Close Date Category Position Information Posting Number F3782PO Department Education/53010 Advertising/Posting Title AMERICAN SIGN LANGUAGE - LECTURER/SENIOR LECTURER FLSA Exempt Position Number 00024952 Employee FTE 1.00 Employee Term (months) 9 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Curriculum Vitae Our Common Ground Statement Optional Documents Other Document (3) ©2019 The University of Vermont – Burlington, VT 05405 – (802) 656-3131 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.uvmjobs.com/postings/88732": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate/Professor Generalist Anesthesiologist",
      "description": "University of Vermont Employment Opportunities | Assistant/Associate/Professor Generalist Anesthesiologist Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UVM Employee Wellness Human Resources UVM Cultural Resource Guide FAQ Clery Act Reports Assistant/Associate/Professor Generalist Anesthesiologist Please carefully review the details of this position below. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job button (or see the Special Instructions below if no button appears). If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark button. The University of Vermont is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, or any other category legally protected by federal or state law. For information on safety and security at the University of Vermont, see the annual security report by clicking on the Clery Act button in the sidebar menu. Finalists for positions at UVM may be subject to a criminal background check. For classified staff positions, actual hiring pay dependent on current competitor market conditions, comparable campus peer(s) at time of hire, and candidate’s experience level and length. Be sure to carefully review and update your application information before submitting an application! Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Posting Details Position will be posted for a minimum of one week, after which it is subject to removal without notice. Advertising Copy Generalist Anesthesiologist at the University of Vermont Medical Center and the University of Vermont Larner College of Medicine The Department of Anesthesiology at The Robert Larner, M.D. College of Medicine at The University of Vermont /University of Vermont Medical Center, in affiliation with the University of Vermont Medical Group, is seeking a full time BC/BE Generalist Attending Anesthesiologist with an interest in supporting our teaching, research, clinical and administrative missions. This is a full-time clinical scholar pathway faculty position at the Assistant, Associate or Professor level based at the University of Vermont Medical Center. Occasional work can be expected at our affiliate hospitals. Preferred candidates will have fellowship training in OB, neuro, regional, pediatric and ICU subspecialties. A comprehensive benefits package is offered that includes the following: · 403b plan participation ( UVM and/or UVMMC ) · Continuing medical education funds based on FTE ( UVMMC ) · Insurance protection including malpractice, health, life and disability ( UVM and/or UVMMC ) · Loan assistance program based on FTE up to $60,000 ( UVMMC ) · Relocation assistance available ( UVMMC ) · Dependent tuition remission ( UVM ) UVMMC is a busy academic hospital with a Level-1 trauma center and we are the only location for tertiary referrals for the catchment area of Vermont and northern upstate New York for all surgeries. We have a large collegial department that consists of Anesthesiologists, Nurse Anesthetists, Anesthesiologist Assistants, a residency program, a pain fellowship and a nurse practitioner. Responsibilities will include clinical care for all subspecialties of anesthesia including pediatrics, neurosurgery, and obstetrics. The University is especially interested in candidates who can contribute to the diversity and excellence of the academic community through their research, teaching, and/or service. Applicants are requested to include in their cover letter information about how they will further this goal. We are located in Burlington, VT. Burlington is a vibrant community located on the shores of Lake Champlain, between the Adirondack and Green Mountains. With year-round recreational opportunities, safe communities and excellent schools, this progressive community has been frequently cited as one of the most livable cities in the U.S. The University of Vermont is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, or any other category legally protected by federal or state law. The University encourages applications from all individuals who will contribute to the diversity and excellence of the institution. Interested candidates must apply online at www.uvmjobs.com (with CV, cover letter and names and addresses of three references). For additional information, please contact Nicholas Cosentino, Provider Recruiter, at Nicholas.consentino@uvmhealth.org . All applications must be submitted online. Anticipated Pay Range Job Location Job Open Date 06/28/2024 Job Close Date Category Position Information Posting Number F3109PO Department Anesthesiology/55500 Advertising/Posting Title Assistant/Associate/Professor Generalist Anesthesiologist FLSA Exempt Position Number 00027108 Employee FTE 1.0 Employee Term (months) 12 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Please specify here where applicable. Enter \"NA\" if not applicable. (Open Ended Question) How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Chronicle of Higher Education HigherEdJobs Inside Higher Ed LinkedIn Seven Days UVM Employee (Please specify below) UVM Employment Web Site Vermont JobLink (Department of Labor) Other (Please specify below) Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter/Letter of Application Optional Documents ©2019 The University of Vermont – Burlington, VT 05405 – (802) 656-3131 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.uvmjobs.com/postings/88731": {
      "title": "Hematology/Oncology - Assistant/Associate/Professor, Clinical Scholar Pathway",
      "description": "University of Vermont Employment Opportunities | Hematology/Oncology - Assistant/Associate/Professor, Clinical Scholar Pathway Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UVM Employee Wellness Human Resources UVM Cultural Resource Guide FAQ Clery Act Reports Hematology/Oncology - Assistant/Associate/Professor, Clinical Scholar Pathway Please carefully review the details of this position below. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job button (or see the Special Instructions below if no button appears). If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark button. The University of Vermont is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, or any other category legally protected by federal or state law. For information on safety and security at the University of Vermont, see the annual security report by clicking on the Clery Act button in the sidebar menu. Finalists for positions at UVM may be subject to a criminal background check. For classified staff positions, actual hiring pay dependent on current competitor market conditions, comparable campus peer(s) at time of hire, and candidate’s experience level and length. Be sure to carefully review and update your application information before submitting an application! Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Posting Details Position will be posted for a minimum of one week, after which it is subject to removal without notice. Advertising Copy Department of Medicine, Division of Hematology/Oncology Ranks: Assistant / Associate / Professor Pathway: Clinical Scholar Pathway The position is full time 1.0 FTE The Department of Medicine, Division of Hematology/Oncology at the Robert Larner, M.D. College of Medicine at The University of Vermont and the University of Vermont Medical Center is pleased to announce a search for an Assistant/Associate/Professor level position in the Clinical Scholar Pathway. Overview The Larner College of Medicine ( LCOM ) at the University of Vermont and University of Vermont Health are seeking an outstanding physician with experience in hematologic malignancies, autologous stem cell transplantation and CAR -T cell therapy to join our academic faculty in the Division of Hematology/Oncology, Department of Medicine. The individual will provide medical care to patients with hematologic disorders in the inpatient and outpatient settings and participate in the UVM Medical Center’s FACT accredited program. The successful candidate must demonstrate a successful record of collaboration and excellence in clinical care, teaching and scholarship. Applicants must be ABIM board eligible in Hematology and/or Medical Oncology and certified if more than 3 years after completion of fellowship. Ideal candidates will possess the experience and skills to support research, advance the educational mission of the University, and/or develop and lead clinical programs. Candidates must be eligible for medical licensure in the State of Vermont, for privileges at UVM Medical Center, and for faculty appointment at the University of Vermont This position offers the opportunity to contribute to a mission-driven academic health system, combining clinical care, education, and research activity in a collaborative environment. Position Highlights Clinical practice at University of Vermont Medical Center Inpatient and outpatient responsibilities Teaching of medical students, residents and fellows Opportunities for research, quality improvement, or academic scholarship Team-based care model Compensation & Benefits Comprehensive benefits including: 403b plan participation ( UVM and UVMH ) Continuing medical education funds based on FTE ( UVMH ) Insurance protection including malpractice, health, life and disability ( UVM and UVMH ) PSLF -eligible Loan Assistance Program (pro-rated by FTE ) up to $60,000 ( UVMH ) Relocation assistance available ( UVMH ) Dependent tuition remission ( UVM ) Medical/Dental/Vision Paid time off Clinical Responsibilities Provide high-quality hematologic care in the ambulatory and inpatient settings Collaborate with advanced practice providers and interdisciplinary teams Participate in call coverage as required Academic Responsibilities Teach and mentor medical students, residents, and fellows Participate in curriculum development and academic programming Engage in scholarly activity (research, publications, QI, etc.) Contribute to the academic mission aligned with LCOM values Qualifications MD/DO (or equivalent) Board Certified or Board Eligible in Hematology/Oncology Eligible for Vermont medical licensure Eligible for DEA certification Demonstrated commitment to clinical excellence, education, and teamwork Rank & Pathway Expectations Appointment at the Assistant, Associate, or Professor level based on experience and academic accomplishments Placement into designated academic pathway based on candidate background and career focus About the Organization The Larner College of Medicine at UVM , the seventh medical school established in the U.S., has a longstanding reputation for educating and training forward-thinking physicians and scientists, fostering groundbreaking research that improves patients’ live, and actively engaging with our local and global communities. Our Larner College of Medicine community upholds the highest standards of professionalism as we follow our passion for lifelong learning and improvement. We demonstrate professionalism through integrity, accountability, compassion, altruism, and social responsibility. We honor the trust our society has placed in us as stewards of the art and science of medicine, relying on cultural humility, kindness, and respect to guide our daily interactions. We expect all members of our community to embrace these principles of professionalism as we strive to conduct and support patient care, research, and education that are second to none. UNIVERSITY OF VERMONT HEALTH The University of Vermont Health ( UVM Health) comprises the University of Vermont Health Medical Group, six hospitals, including the Golisano Children’s Hospital and the UVM Cancer Center, Home Health and Hospice, and 154 outpatient care sites. UVM Health partners work together to offer high quality and high-value care as close to home as possible. Each hospital remains committed to its local community and to the heart and science of medicine: compassionate, personal care shaped by the latest medical advances and delivered by highly skilled experts. UVM Health includes: UVM Health Medical Group | University of Vermont Health University of Vermont Medical Center ( UVMMC ) Central Vermont Medical Center Champlain Valley Physicians Hospital Elizabethtown Community Hospital Alice Hyde Medical Center Porter Medical Center Home Health & Hospice UNIVERSITY OF VERMONT MEDICAL GROUP As the largest physician group in Vermont and northern New York, The UVM Health Medical Group employs 1300 physicians and 600 advanced practice providers, who practice in hospitals, clinics, and digital settings across the health system. The Medical Group providers are committed to bringing expertise and clinical leadership to achieve the health systems goals in patient access, quality, care pathways, patient experience, health equity, population health, clinical trials, and innovation that is rooted in rural communities. About the Community As a UVM Health clinician, you get to live within a community you’ll love to call home with neighbors and friends that truly appreciate the care you provide. Explore what life is like in our practice areas in Vermont and Northern New York: Quality of Life | University of Vermont Health Our Common Ground The University of Vermont is a welcoming, educationally purposeful community committed to creating an inclusive environment that embraces intellectual diversity and global perspectives. We seek to prepare students to be accountable leaders who will bring to their work a grasp of complexity, effective problem-solving and communication skills, and an enduring commitment to learning and ethical conduct. Members of the University of Vermont community embrace and advance the values of Our Common Ground : Respect, Integrity, Innovation, Openness, Justice, and Responsibility. The successful candidate will demonstrate a strong commitment to UVM’s mission and advancing Our Common Ground values through their teaching, service, research, scholarship, or creative arts. Application Instructions Successful candidates will exhibit a strong commitment to the tenets of Our Common Ground and the principles of professionalism . Applicants are requested to include in their cover letter information about how they will enhance the impact of Our Common Ground values and professionalism. Applicants must apply online at: www.uvmjobs.com under Position No. 00023423. Applications must include: CV Cover letter summarizing qualifications and how they will enhance the impact of Our Common Ground values and professionalism Contact information for three references Review of applications will begin immediately. Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Employment is subject to a successful background check. The University of Vermont is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, or any other category legally protected by federal or state law. Anticipated Pay Range Assistant Professor: $375,000 – $425,000 Associate Professor: $400,000 – $475,000 Professor: $450,000 – $500,000 The referenced salary ranges reflect the combined total range based on dual employment by both the University of Vermont and the University of Vermont Health Medical Group. The salary ranges do not include all components of compensation. Therefore, the actual compensation paid to the selected candidate may vary from the salary ranges stated herein. Job Location Burlington, Vermont, United States Job Open Date 10/28/2026 Job Close Date Category Position Information Posting Number F3785PO Department Med-Hematology Oncology/55538 Advertising/Posting Title Hematology/Oncology - Assistant/Associate/Professor, Clinical Scholar Pathway FLSA Exempt Position Number 00023423 Employee FTE 1.0 Employee Term (months) 12 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter/Letter of Application Optional Documents ©2019 The University of Vermont – Burlington, VT 05405 – (802) 656-3131 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.uvmjobs.com/postings/88726": {
      "title": "Full or Associate Professor of Physics",
      "description": "University of Vermont Employment Opportunities | Full or Associate Professor of Physics Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UVM Employee Wellness Human Resources UVM Cultural Resource Guide FAQ Clery Act Reports Full or Associate Professor of Physics Please carefully review the details of this position below. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job button (or see the Special Instructions below if no button appears). If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark button. The University of Vermont is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, or any other category legally protected by federal or state law. For information on safety and security at the University of Vermont, see the annual security report by clicking on the Clery Act button in the sidebar menu. Finalists for positions at UVM may be subject to a criminal background check. For classified staff positions, actual hiring pay dependent on current competitor market conditions, comparable campus peer(s) at time of hire, and candidate’s experience level and length. Be sure to carefully review and update your application information before submitting an application! Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Posting Details Position will be posted for a minimum of one week, after which it is subject to removal without notice. Advertising Copy Full or Associate Professor of Physics Department of Physics, University of Vermont The Department of Physics in the College of Engineering and Mathematical Sciences at the University of Vermont ( UVM ) invites applications for a faculty position at the rank of Professor (with tenure) , or Associate Professor (tenure-track or with tenure) with an anticipated start date of August 23, 2027 . We seek an accomplished scholar with a Ph.D. in Physics or a closely related field and a distinguished record of research, teaching, mentorship, and externally funded scholarship. Candidates should demonstrate excellence in interdisciplinary research, the ability to teach undergraduate and graduate physics courses, and experience mentoring graduate students. Candidates must have strong potential to build new collaborative teams and synergies at the intersections of current areas of research and scholarly strength at the University. The successful candidate will strengthen the department’s research programs in condensed matter physics and biophysics , with preference given to applicants whose expertise includes computational semiconductor materials and physics. Outstanding candidates demonstrating an ability to lead interdisciplinary research efforts in semiconductor science or related topics may be eligible for an endowed professorship. Responsibilities Maintain a vigorous, externally funded research program. Facilitate building highly collaborative interdisciplinary research team. Teach undergraduate and graduate physics courses. Mentor undergraduate, M.S., Ph.D. students, and postdocs. Contribute to departmental, university, and professional service. About the Department and University The Department of Physics offers undergraduate, master’s, and doctoral degree programs within a collaborative, interdisciplinary research environment. Faculty engage in research partnerships across the university, including collaborations with other departments within the College of Engineering and Mathematical Sciences, the Larner College of Medicine, other academic units, research centers and institutes, and local industry including GlobalFoundries. The University of Vermont is an R1 doctoral research university committed to academic excellence, innovation, and student success. The University sits within the United States Economic Development Administration Vermont Gallium Nitride (V-GaN) Tech Hub, focused on design, manufacture, and commercialization of GaN wide bandgap semiconductor technology. The University of Vermont is a welcoming, educationally purposeful community committed to creating an inclusive environment that embraces intellectual diversity and global perspectives. We seek to prepare students to be accountable leaders who will bring to their work a grasp of complexity, effective problem-solving and communication skills, and an enduring commitment to learning and ethical conduct. Members of the University of Vermont community embrace and advance the values of Our Common Ground : Respect, Integrity, Innovation, Openness, Justice, and Responsibility. The successful candidate will demonstrate a strong commitment to UVM’s mission and advancing Our Common Ground values through their teaching, service, research, scholarship, or creative arts. Location Located on the shores of Lake Champlain, Burlington, Vermont offers an exceptional quality of life, a vibrant cultural community, and year-round outdoor recreation. Burlington is within easy reach of Montreal and Boston and is served by Burlington International Airport. Application Process Review of applications will begin December 14, 2026 , and continue until the position is filled. Applicants must apply online at uvmjobs.com (Position #006098) and submit the following documents: Cover letter (maximum 2 pages) Curriculum vitae Research statement (maximum 4 pages) Teaching statement (maximum 2 pages) Statement describing contributions to UVM’s Our Common Ground values through teaching, mentoring, research, and service (maximum 1 page) Contact information for three professional references Reference letters will be requested only from candidates selected for interview. For all applicants, employment is subject to a successful background check. For more information about the position, please contact the Search Committee Chair, Dennis Clougherty at Dennis.Clougherty@uvm.edu . Salary Salary is competitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience. The anticipated nine-month salary range is $125,000-$150,000 depending on rank and experience. Equal Opportunity Statement The University of Vermont is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, or any other category legally protected by federal or state law. Anticipated Pay Range $125,000-$150,000 depending on rank and experience Job Location Burlington, Vermont, United States Job Open Date 10/27/2026 Job Close Date Category Position Information Posting Number F3784PO Department Physics/52270 Advertising/Posting Title Full or Associate Professor of Physics FLSA Exempt Position Number 006098 Employee FTE 1.0 Employee Term (months) 9 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Chronicle of Higher Education HigherEdJobs Inside Higher Ed LinkedIn Seven Days UVM Employee (Please specify below) UVM Employment Web Site Vermont JobLink (Department of Labor) Other (Please specify below) Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter/Letter of Application Teaching Statement Research Statement Our Common Ground Statement Optional Documents ©2019 The University of Vermont – Burlington, VT 05405 – (802) 656-3131 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.uvmjobs.com/postings/88715": {
      "title": "NCUVO Senior Scientific Software Engineer",
      "description": "University of Vermont Employment Opportunities | NCUVO Senior Scientific Software Engineer Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UVM Employee Wellness Human Resources UVM Cultural Resource Guide FAQ Clery Act Reports NCUVO Senior Scientific Software Engineer Please carefully review the details of this position below. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job button (or see the Special Instructions below if no button appears). If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark button. The University of Vermont is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, or any other category legally protected by federal or state law. For information on safety and security at the University of Vermont, see the annual security report by clicking on the Clery Act button in the sidebar menu. Finalists for positions at UVM may be subject to a criminal background check. For classified staff positions, actual hiring pay dependent on current competitor market conditions, comparable campus peer(s) at time of hire, and candidate’s experience level and length. Be sure to carefully review and update your application information before submitting an application! Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Details Advertising/Posting Title NCUVO Senior Scientific Software Engineer Posting Summary The National Connectomics and Ultrastructure Volume Observatory ( NCUVO ) seeks a Senior Scientific Software Engineer to lead development of the computational backbone for a new, NSF -funded high-throughput volume electron microscopy (htvEM) observatory. This role will connect advanced microscopy with petabyte-scale distributed computing, machine learning, visualization, and data stewardship to make complex connectomics and ultrastructure datasets usable by a broad research community. The successful candidate will architect and optimize scalable CPU / GPU workflows; evaluate and integrate open-source tools; develop new software when existing solutions are insufficient; establish rigorous engineering and validation practices for both manual and frontier model-based software development; and collaborate with scientific and computing partners at UVM and nationally. This is a senior individual-contributor role for an expert who can translate emerging research methods into dependable production systems, and convene collaborative technical activities such as NCUVO hackathons. The position will report directly to the NCUVO Director and will have functional supervision of technical staff. The successful candidate will be a recognized expert in the field who is expected to liaise with external partners in the National Center for Microscopy and Imaging Research ( NCMIR ), the University of California San Diego ( UCSD ), and the San Diego Supercomputer Center ( SDSC ), and with developers of open-source software components used in the NCUVO pipeline. Minimum Qualifications (or equivalent combination of education and experience) * PhD in engineering, computer science, biomedical engineering, computational science, data science, neuroscience, physical science, or a closely related field, and at least 10 years of related experience in scientific software engineering, research-computing, microscopy data processing, or an equivalent combination of advanced education and relevant experience. * Expert knowledge and at least ten years of experience managing and processing large microscopy datasets in the approximately 100-terabyte to 1-petabyte range using large-scale distributed computing environments. Experience with electron microscopy or volume electron microscopy is strongly preferred. * Demonstrated experience independently architecting, developing, deploying, integrating, and sustaining modular production software and custom pipeline components for specialized research needs across complex computing environments. * Demonstrated experience with high-performance or distributed computing, including parallel CPU and GPU workflows, and with profiling and optimizing runtime, memory, storage, input/output, and network performance for very large datasets. * Advanced programming experience in Python and at least one compiled or numerical language such as C, C++, or MATLAB in a Linux environment. Experience with collaborative software-engineering practices, including version control, testing, code review, documentation, release management, and reproducible workflows. * Demonstrated experience with machine learning and image processing, including alignment, registration, segmentation, feature detection, or comparable computer-vision problems. * Demonstrated ability to use frontier AI models effectively and responsibly to support development of maintainable, reliable, testable, and extensible software or pipeline components. * Demonstrated ability to evaluate emerging software from the research community; reproduce or validate relevant results; assess fitness for scientific and production use; and deploy appropriate components within a supported software environment. * Demonstrated ability to investigate and resolve undefined, highly complex technical problems; work autonomously with high-level direction; establish technical plans and standards; and coordinate and influence work across institutional, scientific, technical, vendor, and external partner groups. * Demonstrated experience providing technical leadership, guidance, coaching, or mentoring to staff, students, or other contributors. Experience planning and facilitating collaborative technical-development events such as hackathons, code sprints, or design workshops. Effective written and oral communication skills. Desirable Qualifications Extensive experience with serial-section or volume electron microscopy, connectomics, petabyte-scale scientific imaging, ground-truth annotation and model evaluation, scientific visualization, research publications, open-source scientific software, commercial segmentation services, and multi-institutional team science. Anticipated Pay Range $160,000-$175,000 Other Information Special Conditions A probationary period may be required, Contingent on continued funding, Occasional evening and/or weekends required (if non-exempt position, may result in overtime), This position is eligible for a hybrid schedule with an option to split time between campus and elsewhere, in accordance with the university telecommuting policy, Background Check required for this position FLSA Exempt Union Position Yes, UVMSU Posting Details Position will be posted for a minimum of one week, after which it is subject to removal without notice. Job Location Burlington, Vermont, United States Job Open Date 10/27/2026 Job Close Date (Jobs close at 11:59 PM EST.) Open Until Filled No Our Common Ground Statement The University of Vermont is a welcoming, educationally purposeful community committed to creating an inclusive environment that embraces intellectual diversity and global perspectives. We seek to prepare students to be accountable leaders who will bring to their work a grasp of complexity, effective problem-solving and communication skills, and an enduring commitment to learning and ethical conduct. Members of the University of Vermont community embrace and advance the values of Our Common Ground: Respect, Integrity, Innovation, Openness, Justice, and Responsibility. Staff play a critical role in this effort and the successful candidate will demonstrate a strong commitment to UVM’s mission and advancing Our Common Ground values through the execution of their job duties. Position Information Position Title Systems Engineering PC5 X Posting Number S6377PO Department Neurological Sciences/55800 Position Number 00028035 Percent of Full-Time 1.0 Standard Hours at 1.0 FTE 37.5 Term (months per year) 12 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application Optional Documents Curriculum Vitae ©2019 The University of Vermont – Burlington, VT 05405 – (802) 656-3131 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.uvmjobs.com/postings/88711": {
      "title": "NCUVO Senior Project Manager",
      "description": "University of Vermont Employment Opportunities | NCUVO Senior Project Manager Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UVM Employee Wellness Human Resources UVM Cultural Resource Guide FAQ Clery Act Reports NCUVO Senior Project Manager Please carefully review the details of this position below. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job button (or see the Special Instructions below if no button appears). If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark button. The University of Vermont is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, or any other category legally protected by federal or state law. For information on safety and security at the University of Vermont, see the annual security report by clicking on the Clery Act button in the sidebar menu. Finalists for positions at UVM may be subject to a criminal background check. For classified staff positions, actual hiring pay dependent on current competitor market conditions, comparable campus peer(s) at time of hire, and candidate’s experience level and length. Be sure to carefully review and update your application information before submitting an application! Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Details Advertising/Posting Title NCUVO Senior Project Manager Posting Summary NCUVO seeks a Senior Project Manager to lead the operational and business management of a complex NSF -funded research-infrastructure cooperative agreement. This is not a conventional departmental project-coordinator role. The position will integrate project planning, sponsor relations, financial stewardship, risk and quality management, governance, reviews, procurement, partner coordination, and external engagement across a national network of universities, computing centers, scientific collaborators, advisors, and commercial vendors. The Senior Project Manager will be the primary operational liaison with NSF ; will coordinate the work and deliverables of scientific and technical teams without personally executing those technical tasks; and must be able to translate between sponsor requirements, institutional processes, and advanced scientific and engineering activities. The role requires substantial autonomy, excellent judgment, and sufficient scientific fluency to manage a sophisticated high-throughput volume-electron-microscopy infrastructure initiative. Minimum Qualifications (or equivalent combination of education and experience) * Bachelor’s degree in a bioscience, biomedical engineering, engineering, research administration, project or program management, business or public administration, or a related field, and at least four years of progressively responsible experience managing complex projects or programs, including substantial experience in an academic research, scientific infrastructure, government, or similarly complex environment, or an equivalent combination of education and experience. * Demonstrated experience independently managing federally sponsored projects (preferably multi-institutional), through planning, execution, monitoring, formal review, change, and closeout. Experience coordinating work across organizations and disciplines where contributors do not report directly to the project manager. * Demonstrated experience serving as a principal operational contact for a federal sponsor or comparable external authority, including leadership of deadline-driven technical and financial reporting, review preparation, information requests, corrective-action tracking, and sponsor communications. * Demonstrated experience with project controls, including integrated schedules, work breakdown structures, budgets and forecasts, risk and opportunity management, quality systems, performance metrics, issue escalation, change control, decision records, and document management. * Demonstrated experience with business administration for complex research or technical programs, including procurement, contracts, subawards, consultants, vendors, equipment, software licenses, compliance, internal controls, and auditable project records. * Sufficient scientific and technical knowledge to understand and communicate about advanced bioscience, microscopy, imaging, research computing, or data-intensive workflows; translate among investigators, engineers, administrators, sponsors, vendors, and institutional leadership; and recognize the operational implications of technical decisions. * Demonstrated ability to work autonomously with high-level direction; exercise judgment on complex and often undefined issues; influence cross-functional and external stakeholders; organize information from multiple institutions; and convert complex requirements into clear plans, decisions, reports, and accountable follow-through. * Experience planning and facilitating advisory boards, scientific or technical reviews, collaborator meetings, invited-speaker series, workshops, training programs, conferences, or comparable multi-stakeholder activities. Excellent written, oral, interpersonal, negotiation, and facilitation skills. *Proficiency with project-management, financial-tracking, document-management, collaboration, spreadsheet, presentation, and reporting tools. Desirable Qualifications Master’s degree or PhD in a bioscience, biomedical engineering, engineering, or related scientific field; eight or more years of relevant experience; experience independently managing multi-institutional federally sponsored projects or cooperative agreements, or serving as a principal operational contact for a federal sponsor; recognized project-management or research-administration credential; direct experience with NSF cooperative agreements, major research infrastructure, or the NSF Research Infrastructure Guide; experience with electron microscopy, imaging facilities, research computing, data stewardship, or national research resources; and experience developing sustainability models and future funding proposals. Anticipated Pay Range $84,000-$104,000 Other Information Special Conditions A probationary period may be required, Contingent on continued funding, Occasional evening and/or weekends required (if non-exempt position, may result in overtime), This position is eligible for a hybrid schedule with an option to split time between campus and elsewhere, in accordance with the university telecommuting policy, Background Check required for this position FLSA Exempt Union Position Yes, UVMSU Posting Details Position will be posted for a minimum of one week, after which it is subject to removal without notice. Job Location Burlington, Vermont, United States Job Open Date 10/27/2026 Job Close Date (Jobs close at 11:59 PM EST.) Open Until Filled No Our Common Ground Statement The University of Vermont is a welcoming, educationally purposeful community committed to creating an inclusive environment that embraces intellectual diversity and global perspectives. We seek to prepare students to be accountable leaders who will bring to their work a grasp of complexity, effective problem-solving and communication skills, and an enduring commitment to learning and ethical conduct. Members of the University of Vermont community embrace and advance the values of Our Common Ground: Respect, Integrity, Innovation, Openness, Justice, and Responsibility. Staff play a critical role in this effort and the successful candidate will demonstrate a strong commitment to UVM’s mission and advancing Our Common Ground values through the execution of their job duties. Position Information Position Title Project/Prgm Mgmt PC4 X Posting Number S6376PO Department Neurological Sciences/55800 Position Number 00028033 Percent of Full-Time 1.0 Standard Hours at 1.0 FTE 37.5 Term (months per year) 12 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application Optional Documents Curriculum Vitae ©2019 The University of Vermont – Burlington, VT 05405 – (802) 656-3131 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
