    "https://www.uvmjobs.com/postings/88682": {
      "title": "Rural Gerontology, Healthy Aging and Clinical Innovation- Assistant/Associate/Full Professor (Research or Tenure Pathway)",
      "description": "University of Vermont Employment Opportunities | Rural Gerontology, Healthy Aging and Clinical Innovation- Assistant/Associate/Full Professor (Research or Tenure Pathway) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UVM Employee Wellness Human Resources UVM Cultural Resource Guide FAQ Clery Act Reports Rural Gerontology, Healthy Aging and Clinical Innovation- Assistant/Associate/Full Professor (Research or Tenure Pathway) Please carefully review the details of this position below. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job button (or see the Special Instructions below if no button appears). If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark button. The University of Vermont is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, or any other category legally protected by federal or state law. For information on safety and security at the University of Vermont, see the annual security report by clicking on the Clery Act button in the sidebar menu. Finalists for positions at UVM may be subject to a criminal background check. For classified staff positions, actual hiring pay dependent on current competitor market conditions, comparable campus peer(s) at time of hire, and candidate’s experience level and length. Be sure to carefully review and update your application information before submitting an application! Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Posting Details Position will be posted for a minimum of one week, after which it is subject to removal without notice. Advertising Copy The Robert Larner MD College of Medicine at the University of Vermont and The University of Vermont Health Medical Group are leaders in patient care, medical education and research. The Department of Medicine has initiated a search for a faculty position at the Assistant/Associate Professor/ Professor level (Research Scholar or Tenure Pathway) . We are seeking an outstanding scientist with an established research program and a commitment to gerontology, healthy aging and clinical innovation in the context of rural health. The faculty member will develop an independent, externally funded research program focused on promoting healthy aging, maintaining independence and quality of life, and advancing innovative models of care delivery for older adults living in rural settings. Research may span clinical innovation, aging services, technology-enabled care, population health, implementation science, and health system transformation. Strong collaborative opportunities exist with rapidly growing programs across UVM Health, the Larner College of Medicine and the University of Vermont. Qualifications Ph.D., Dr.P.H., M.D., D.O., D.N.P., Sc.D., or equivalent doctoral degree in gerontology, medicine, public health, epidemiology, health services research, nursing, sociology, psychology, implementation science, or a related field. Demonstrated scholarship related to aging, population health, clinical innovation, health services research, caregiving or rural health. Evidence of potential for or success in obtaining extramural funding from NIH (particularly NIA ), HRSA , AHRQ , PCORI , foundations, or other funding agencies. Strong record of peer-reviewed publications commensurate with academic rank. Demonstrated commitment to collaborative and interdisciplinary research. The University of Vermont is a welcoming, educationally purposeful community committed to creating an inclusive environment that embraces intellectual diversity and global perspectives. We seek to prepare students to be accountable leaders who will bring to their work a grasp of complexity, effective problem-solving and communication skills, and an enduring commitment to learning and ethical conduct. Members of the University of Vermont community embrace and advance the values of Our Common Ground : Respect, Integrity, Innovation, Openness, Justice, and Responsibility. The successful candidate will demonstrate a strong commitment to UVM’s mission and advancing Our Common Ground values through their teaching, service, research, scholarship, or creative arts. Successful candidates will exhibit a strong commitment to the tenets of Our Common Ground and the principles of professionalism . Applicants are required to submit a separate statement detailing how they would enhance the impact of Our Common Ground values and professionalism. The University of Vermont is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, or any other category legally protected by federal or state law. The University of Vermont offers an outstanding benefits package including paid vacation, holidays, and sick days, medical/dental/vision coverage, employer-funded retirement plan options. Applicants must apply online at: www.uvmjobs.com under Position No. 00028024. Applications must include: · CV · Cover letter · Contact information for three references · A separate statement detailing how you will enhance the values of Our Common Ground and Professionalism. Questions about this opportunity may be directed to: Fred Ko, MD Director, Center on Aging Division Chief of Geriatrics Email: fred.ko@med.uvm.edu Review of applications will begin immediately. Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Employment is subject to a successful background check. Anticipated Pay Range Assistant Professor: $110,000-$125,000 Associate Professor: $120,000-$160,000 Professor: $155,000-$240,000 Job Location Burlington, Vermont, United States Job Open Date 10/13/2026 Job Close Date Category Position Information Posting Number F3777PO Department Med-Geriatrics/55532 Advertising/Posting Title Rural Gerontology, Healthy Aging and Clinical Innovation- Assistant/Associate/Full Professor (Research or Tenure Pathway) FLSA Exempt Position Number 00028024 Employee FTE 1.0 Employee Term (months) 12 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Please specify here where applicable. Enter \"NA\" if not applicable. (Open Ended Question) How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Chronicle of Higher Education HigherEdJobs Inside Higher Ed LinkedIn Seven Days UVM Employee (Please specify below) UVM Employment Web Site Vermont JobLink (Department of Labor) Other (Please specify below) Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter/Letter of Application Our Common Ground Statement Optional Documents Other Document (1) ©2019 The University of Vermont – Burlington, VT 05405 – (802) 656-3131 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.uvmjobs.com/postings/88680": {
      "title": "Digital Health and Clinical Informatics- Assistant/Associate/Full Professor (Research or Tenure Pathway)",
      "description": "University of Vermont Employment Opportunities | Digital Health and Clinical Informatics- Assistant/Associate/Full Professor (Research or Tenure Pathway) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UVM Employee Wellness Human Resources UVM Cultural Resource Guide FAQ Clery Act Reports Digital Health and Clinical Informatics- Assistant/Associate/Full Professor (Research or Tenure Pathway) Please carefully review the details of this position below. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job button (or see the Special Instructions below if no button appears). If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark button. The University of Vermont is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, or any other category legally protected by federal or state law. For information on safety and security at the University of Vermont, see the annual security report by clicking on the Clery Act button in the sidebar menu. Finalists for positions at UVM may be subject to a criminal background check. For classified staff positions, actual hiring pay dependent on current competitor market conditions, comparable campus peer(s) at time of hire, and candidate’s experience level and length. Be sure to carefully review and update your application information before submitting an application! Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Posting Details Position will be posted for a minimum of one week, after which it is subject to removal without notice. Advertising Copy The Robert Larner MD College of Medicine at the University of Vermont and The University of Vermont Health Medical Group are leaders in patient care, medical education and research. The Department of Medicine has initiated a search for a faculty position at the Assistant/Associate Professor/ Professor level (Research Scholar or Tenure Track Pathway) . We are seeking an outstanding scientist with an established research program and a commitment to digital and clinical informatics in the context of rural health. The faculty member will develop an independent, externally funded research program focused on the application of digital technologies, telehealth, data science, artificial intelligence, and/or clinical informatics to improve health outcomes, health care delivery, and access to care for rural populations. Strong collaborative opportunities exist with rapidly growing programs across UVM Health, the Larner College of Medicine and the University of Vermont. Qualifications: Ph.D., M.D., Dr.P.H., Pharm.D., or equivalent doctoral degree in biomedical informatics, clinical informatics, health services research, computer science, public health, data science, medicine, nursing, or a related field. Demonstrated scholarly achievement in digital health, clinical informatics, telehealth, implementation science, or related areas. Evidence of potential for or achievement in securing extramural funding from NIH , AHRQ , PCORI , HRSA , CDC , NSF , foundations, or other funding agencies. Strong record of peer-reviewed publications commensurate with academic rank. Commitment to interdisciplinary team science and collaborative research. The University of Vermont is a welcoming, educationally purposeful community committed to creating an inclusive environment that embraces intellectual diversity and global perspectives. We seek to prepare students to be accountable leaders who will bring to their work a grasp of complexity, effective problem-solving and communication skills, and an enduring commitment to learning and ethical conduct. Members of the University of Vermont community embrace and advance the values of Our Common Ground : Respect, Integrity, Innovation, Openness, Justice, and Responsibility. The successful candidate will demonstrate a strong commitment to UVM’s mission and advancing Our Common Ground values through their teaching, service, research, scholarship, or creative arts. Successful candidates will exhibit a strong commitment to the tenets of Our Common Ground and the principles of professionalism . Applicants are required to submit a separate statement detailing how they would enhance the impact of Our Common Ground values and professionalism. The University of Vermont is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, or any other category legally protected by federal or state law. The University of Vermont offers an outstanding benefits package including paid vacation, holidays, and sick days, medical/dental/vision coverage, and employer-funded retirement plan options. Applicants must apply online at: www.uvmjobs.com under Position No. 00028025. Applications must include: · CV · Cover letter · Contact information for three references · A separate statement detailing how you will enhance the values of Our Common Ground and Professionalism. Questions about this opportunity may be directed to: Erika Ziller, PhD Director, Northeast Rural Health Research Center Director Health Services Research Email: erika.ziller@med.uvm.edu Review of applications will begin immediately. Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Employment is subject to a successful background check. Anticipated Pay Range Assistant Professor: $110,000-$125,000 Associate Professor: $120,000-$160,000 Professor: $155,000-$240,000 Job Location Burlington, Vermont, United States Job Open Date 10/13/2026 Job Close Date Category Position Information Posting Number F3778PO Department Med-Gen Internal Med/55536 Advertising/Posting Title Digital Health and Clinical Informatics- Assistant/Associate/Full Professor (Research or Tenure Pathway) FLSA Exempt Position Number 00028025 Employee FTE 1.0 Employee Term (months) 12 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Please specify here where applicable. Enter \"NA\" if not applicable. (Open Ended Question) How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Chronicle of Higher Education HigherEdJobs Inside Higher Ed LinkedIn Seven Days UVM Employee (Please specify below) UVM Employment Web Site Vermont JobLink (Department of Labor) Other (Please specify below) Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter/Letter of Application Our Common Ground Statement Optional Documents Other Document (1) ©2019 The University of Vermont – Burlington, VT 05405 – (802) 656-3131 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.uvmjobs.com/postings/88679": {
      "title": "Faculty Relations Administrator",
      "description": "University of Vermont Employment Opportunities | Faculty Relations Administrator Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UVM Employee Wellness Human Resources UVM Cultural Resource Guide FAQ Clery Act Reports Faculty Relations Administrator Please carefully review the details of this position below. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job button (or see the Special Instructions below if no button appears). If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark button. The University of Vermont is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, or any other category legally protected by federal or state law. For information on safety and security at the University of Vermont, see the annual security report by clicking on the Clery Act button in the sidebar menu. Finalists for positions at UVM may be subject to a criminal background check. For classified staff positions, actual hiring pay dependent on current competitor market conditions, comparable campus peer(s) at time of hire, and candidate’s experience level and length. Be sure to carefully review and update your application information before submitting an application! Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Details Advertising/Posting Title Faculty Relations Administrator Posting Summary Provide operational, policy, procedural and transactional oversight for sensitive and highly confidential personnel documents related to faculty affairs actions in the College of Medicine. Provide interpretation, training, guidance, and problem solving strategies to Department Chairs and administrators and support staff and advise Associate Dean, Dean and other senior leaderships within LCOM on operational protocol. Ensure compliance with reappointment/promotion policies and procedures. Consistently exercise independent judgment in advising department leadership and administrative staff to meet institutional deadlines and obligations to avoid risk of institutional liability. Evaluate needs, recommend and formulate procedural process changes. Report to Associate Dean for Faculty Affairs. Minimum Qualifications (or equivalent combination of education and experience) Bachelor’s degree in a related field and one to three years of related experience required. Effective organizational, interpersonal, communication and writing skills required. Proficiency in MS Office applications and experience with data and survey platforms such as REDCap, Qualtrics, or Ironclad required. Demonstrated ability to use software tools to summarize and manipulate large data sets required. Desirable Qualifications Experience with enterprise systems such as PeopleSoft and PeopleAdmin highly desirable. Experience supporting administrative leaders and coordinating institutional initiatives within an academic medical college is desirable. Anticipated Pay Range $60,000-$65,000 Other Information A four-month probationary period is required. Special Conditions Occasional evening and/or weekends required (if non-exempt position, may result in overtime), This position is eligible for a hybrid schedule with an option to split time between campus and elsewhere, in accordance with the university telecommuting policy, Background Check required for this position FLSA Exempt Union Position No Posting Details Position will be posted for a minimum of one week, after which it is subject to removal without notice. Job Location Burlington, Vermont, United States Job Open Date 10/23/2026 Job Close Date (Jobs close at 11:59 PM EST.) Open Until Filled No Our Common Ground Statement The University of Vermont is a welcoming, educationally purposeful community committed to creating an inclusive environment that embraces intellectual diversity and global perspectives. We seek to prepare students to be accountable leaders who will bring to their work a grasp of complexity, effective problem-solving and communication skills, and an enduring commitment to learning and ethical conduct. Members of the University of Vermont community embrace and advance the values of Our Common Ground: Respect, Integrity, Innovation, Openness, Justice, and Responsibility. Staff play a critical role in this effort and the successful candidate will demonstrate a strong commitment to UVM’s mission and advancing Our Common Ground values through the execution of their job duties. Position Information Position Title Academic Affairs PC3 X Posting Number S6372PO Department COM Office of Faculty/55038 Position Number 002586 Percent of Full-Time 1.0 Standard Hours at 1.0 FTE 37.5 Term (months per year) 12 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Please specify here where applicable. Enter \"NA\" if not applicable. (Open Ended Question) How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Chronicle of Higher Education HigherEdJobs Inside Higher Ed LinkedIn Seven Days UVM Employee (Please specify below) UVM Employment Web Site Vermont JobLink (Department of Labor) Other (Please specify below) Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application Optional Documents ©2019 The University of Vermont – Burlington, VT 05405 – (802) 656-3131 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
