      "title": "Finance Administrator",
      "description": "University of Vermont Employment Opportunities | Finance Administrator Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UVM Employee Wellness Human Resources UVM Cultural Resource Guide FAQ Clery Act Reports Finance Administrator Please carefully review the details of this position below. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job button (or see the Special Instructions below if no button appears). If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark button. The University of Vermont is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, or any other category legally protected by federal or state law. For information on safety and security at the University of Vermont, see the annual security report by clicking on the Clery Act button in the sidebar menu. Finalists for positions at UVM may be subject to a criminal background check. For classified staff positions, actual hiring pay dependent on current competitor market conditions, comparable campus peer(s) at time of hire, and candidate’s experience level and length. Be sure to carefully review and update your application information before submitting an application! Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Details Advertising/Posting Title Finance Administrator Posting Summary The Finance Administrator provides primary financial and business operations support to the Office of Medical Education, including Admissions, Curriculum across educational sites, the Clinical Simulation Laboratory, Medical Student Services, the Teaching Academy, and Continuing Medical and Interprofessional Education. The position also provides designated financial support to other Larner College of Medicine units, including the Office of Public Relations and the Center for Aging. The Finance Administrator oversees budgeting, financial forecasting, purchasing, receivables, and operational processes across multiple programs and funding sources with annual budgets exceeding $8 million. The position partners closely with the Dean’s Office Financial Director and OME Human Resources Administrator to support fiscal planning, compliance, and resource management. The Finance Administrator serves as a financial advisor and liaison to leadership, student organizations, and affiliated programs by providing budget guidance, financial analysis, policy interpretation, and funding recommendations. The position also manages purchasing and vendor relations, supports grant administration, prepares financial reports, and communicates budget trends and potential shortfalls to senior leadership to promote effective stewardship of organizational resources. Minimum Qualifications (or equivalent combination of education and experience) Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree and two to four years of relevant experience in financial administration, business operations, or a related field, including demonstrated leadership or management experience, required. Ability to work independently Effective analytical, reasoning, judgment, organizational, problem-solving, and computer skills Effective interpersonal and communication skills required. Desirable Qualifications Desirable Qualifications: Familiarity with PeopleSoft is highly desirable. Proficiency with Microsoft Office Suite and advanced proficiency in Microsoft Excel, including financial modeling, data analysis, and reporting, are preferred. Experience in financial administration within higher education, healthcare, or a similarly complex organization is also preferred. Anticipated Pay Range $72,000-$78,000 Other Information Special Conditions A probationary period may be required, This position is eligible for a hybrid schedule with an option to split time between campus and elsewhere, in accordance with the university telecommuting policy, Background Check required for this position FLSA Exempt Union Position Yes, UVMSU Posting Details Position will be posted for a minimum of one week, after which it is subject to removal without notice. Job Location Burlington, Vermont, United States Job Open Date 10/23/2026 Job Close Date (Jobs close at 11:59 PM EST.) Open Until Filled No Our Common Ground Statement The University of Vermont is a welcoming, educationally purposeful community committed to creating an inclusive environment that embraces intellectual diversity and global perspectives. We seek to prepare students to be accountable leaders who will bring to their work a grasp of complexity, effective problem-solving and communication skills, and an enduring commitment to learning and ethical conduct. Members of the University of Vermont community embrace and advance the values of Our Common Ground: Respect, Integrity, Innovation, Openness, Justice, and Responsibility. Staff play a critical role in this effort and the successful candidate will demonstrate a strong commitment to UVM’s mission and advancing Our Common Ground values through the execution of their job duties. Position Information Position Title Fiscal Ops & Bus Mgmt PC3 X Posting Number S6371PO Department COM Ofc of Med Ed/55024 Position Number 00028034 Percent of Full-Time 1.00 Standard Hours at 1.0 FTE 37.5 Term (months per year) 12 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Please specify here where applicable. Enter \"NA\" if not applicable. (Open Ended Question) How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Chronicle of Higher Education HigherEdJobs Inside Higher Ed LinkedIn Seven Days UVM Employee (Please specify below) UVM Employment Web Site Vermont JobLink (Department of Labor) Other (Please specify below) Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application Optional Documents ©2019 The University of Vermont – Burlington, VT 05405 – (802) 656-3131 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
