      "title": "CAS HR &amp; Faculty Actions Specialist",
      "description": "University of Vermont Employment Opportunities | CAS HR &amp; Faculty Actions Specialist Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UVM Employee Wellness Human Resources UVM Cultural Resource Guide FAQ Clery Act Reports CAS HR & Faculty Actions Specialist Please carefully review the details of this position below. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job button (or see the Special Instructions below if no button appears). If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark button. The University of Vermont is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, or any other category legally protected by federal or state law. For information on safety and security at the University of Vermont, see the annual security report by clicking on the Clery Act button in the sidebar menu. Finalists for positions at UVM may be subject to a criminal background check. For classified staff positions, actual hiring pay dependent on current competitor market conditions, comparable campus peer(s) at time of hire, and candidate’s experience level and length. Be sure to carefully review and update your application information before submitting an application! Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Details Advertising/Posting Title CAS HR & Faculty Actions Specialist Posting Summary The CAS HR/Fac Actions Specialist will coordinate and support specialized human resources and administrative functions for academic departments within the College of Arts and Sciences, College Administrative Services ( CAS – CAS ). Provide administrative and procedural support for faculty actions, including reappointment, promotion and tenure ( RPT ), and sabbatical leave; support Schedule of Courses planning and development; and assist with faculty and staff recruitment, hiring, and other personnel activities. Interpret and communicate university policies, procedures, and applicable collective bargaining agreements, providing guidance to faculty, department administrators, and academic leaders while collaborating with campus partners to ensure the accurate and timely processing of actions. As part of a collaborative team supporting a cooperative model, serve as a primary point of contact for inquiries, facilitate clear and consistent communication, coordinate workflows, maintain records, and assist in resolving procedural issues. Monitor processes, identify opportunities for improvement, and ensure compliance with department, college, university, and collective bargaining agreement requirements. Minimum Qualifications (or equivalent combination of education and experience) Bachelor’s degree in human resources, business administration, or related field and two to four years of related experience in an administrative setting required. Proficiency with Microsoft Office applications, (especially Excel, Word), and database applications required, and familiarity with internet resources required. Effective analytical, problem solving, organizational, communication, interpersonal, team-collaboration, and writing skills required. Attention to detail and accuracy required. Demonstrated experience and commitment to overall customer service and ability to discern and maintain confidential information required. Desirable Qualifications Experience using human resource and enrollment/student management systems, such as PeopleSoft, PeopleAdmin, and Banner highly desirable. Anticipated Pay Range $27.50 - $28.97/hour Other Information Applicants are asked to apply online. Please provide a cover letter, resume and contact information for three professional references. The College of Arts and Sciences ( CAS ) at the University of 